        text: "[Condensed paraphrase] When Prince Vladimir ruled in Kyiv he set idols on the hill: Perun of wood with silver head, and Hors, Dazhbog, Stribog, Simargl and Mokosh. The people sacrificed to them, calling their sons and daughters to the hill, and the heathen gods of the old Russians were honored with offerings."
