      en: "Ameta, hunting wild pigs, finds a coconut in a boar's tusk; a girl, Hainuwele, grows from it in three days bearing valuables in her palms; at the maro dance the men crowd around her until she sinks into the ground; Ameta digs up her body and cuts it into pieces, which, buried, become the clans' food-plants \u2014 the dema myth of culture rising from murder.",
