        text: "Condensed paraphrase of the maro dance (Jensen 1939): At the nine-day maro dance the men danced in a circle around Hainuwele, who stood at the center; each night the circle pressed closer; on the ninth night she sank into the ground; Ameta dug her up and, following a spirit's? instruction, cut her body into pieces and buried them; from the pieces grew the plants \u2014 the yams, coconuts, and tubers that feed the clans. Not verbatim.",
