    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "The fetter called Gleipnir the dwarfs made of six things: the footfall of a cat, the roots of a mountain, the sinews of a bear, the breath of a fish, the spittle of a bird, and a woman's beard. These things went into the band, and that is why they exist no longer - a cat's footfall, a woman's beard, the roots of mountains, the breath of fish, the spittle of birds cannot be found now.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Snorri, Gylfaginning ch. 34 (Brodeur 1916); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "The wolf would not be bound unless one of the gods set his hand in its mouth as a pledge. Each god looked at the other, until T\xFDr put forth his right hand and laid it in the wolf's jaws. Then the band was fastened, and when the wolf strained, it gripped the harder; he bit, and T\xFDr lost his hand at the wrist - and the gods thrust a sword into the wolf's mouth, hilt upward, and bound him to a rock in the lake, where he waits for Ragnarok.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Snorri, Gylfaginning ch. 34 (Brodeur 1916); not verbatim."
      }
    ]
