    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Hel's hall is called Eljudnir, her dish 'Hunger', her knife 'Famine', her thralls 'Sloth' and 'Sourness', her bed 'Sickness'; her gates are called 'Stumbling-block', and to those sent to her she apportions all abodes. She is half blue-black and half flesh-colored, easily known, and more downcast and fierce in look than the others.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Snorri, Gylfaginning ch. 34 (Brodeur 1916); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "The road lies northward and downward, nine nights' ride; the river Gjoll runs by the iron gates of Hel, and the bridge Gjallarbru, roofed with shining gold, crosses it. The maiden Modgudr keeps the bridge: five companies of dead rode over, and it rang less under them; but a living rider makes it thunder like gold.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Snorri, Gylfaginning ch. 49 (Brodeur 1916); not verbatim."
      }
    ]
