        text: "Regin bade Sigurd roast the dragon's heart; and as he roasted it, Sigurd touched it with his finger and burned it, and set the finger in his mouth - and at that moment he understood the speech of birds. The nuthatches in the tree above counseled him: Regin plots his death; eat the heart yourself and drink the blood, and take the treasure - then wisdom shall wax in you. Sigurd beheaded Regin as he slept, loaded Grani with the hoard, and rode the Rhine-road with the ring whose end is death.",
