        text: "Gudrun, hardened like iron quenched in water, egged her two sons to avenge their sister Svanhild, trampled by horses at King Jormunrek's command. On the road Erp, their half-brother, said he would help them as one hand helps the other; they scoffed and killed him.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Hamdismal st. 1-6 and Volsunga saga ch. 43 (Bellows; Morris & Magnusson); not verbatim."
