        id: "1",
        text: "Harald Wartooth declared war rather than waste with age: better, he said, to die in glory on the field than to rot on the bed; the battle was scheduled as a good death. The armies met at Br\xE1vellir and fought seven days by drawn ranks; Starkadr fought on both sides. An old one-eyed charioteer drove Harald's chariot into the thick of the field and cast his club, and the king died of the blow - and the charioteer was Odin, harvesting both armies for the army of Ragnarok.",
