        text: "On the battle-night, when the enemy attacked the king's hall, Bodvar Bjarki was nowhere in the field - but a huge bear fought at the front of the king's banner, slaying with one paw-blow more men than five champions. The queen woke Bodvar sleeping in his bed and demanded he fight; the bear vanished the moment its sleeper woke, and Bodvar said: 'you have deprived the king of much victory - the bear was my shape, sent while I slept; now it is gone.'",
