        text: "Ingolf held a great sacrifice to learn whether he should settle in the new land, and took the high-seat pillars of his hall, dedicating them to the gods, and threw them overboard, vowing to settle where they came ashore. After a three-year search along the coast he found the pillars in the south-west, built his hall there, and named the bay Reykjavik, smoke-bay, for the steam rising from the hot springs.",
