        id: "1",
        text: "At the Yule-feast the first cup should be dedicated to Odin for the king's victory, then cups to Njord and Freyja for plenty and peace; and over the memory-cup men vowed deeds of valor. The bonders pressed the king to drink to Thor and eat the sacrificial horse-flesh; the bishop's cross over the cup was read as the hammer-sign, and the king drank - but at last he only swallowed the fat that ran from a piece of horse-liver, and drank no more.",
