        id: "1",
        text: "Egill took a hazel-pole, set a horse's head on it, went on a crag that looked inland, and spoke: 'Here I set up a nithing-pole, and turn this nithing against King Erik and Queen Gunnhildr.' He turned the horse's head landward and said: 'and I turn this nithing against the land-spirits that dwell in this land, that they may all go astray and find no rest till they drive Erik and Gunnhildr from the land.'",
