        text: "Svafrlami forced the dwarfs Dvalin and Durin to forge him a sword with a gold hilt, never failing of blow nor rusting, that would cut stone and iron as though it were cloth. At the gate the king said the work was as he had bade; and the dwarfs answered: 'the sword shall be the death of a man each time it is drawn, and three shameful deeds with it, and it shall be thy own bane' - and they went into the rock.",
