      en: "Two granite monoliths at Jelling, raised by two generations of kings, are Denmark's conversion-monument and dynastic charter. The smaller (DR 41): King Gorm raises it in memory of Thyra his wife, called 'Denmark's ornament'. The larger (DR 42), often called the 'certificate of baptism of Denmark': King Harald raises the great stone with the carved figure of Christ in the style of the cross-slabs, and claims in its formula to have 'won for himself all of Denmark and Norway and made the Danes Christian'.",
