        id: "1",
        text: "Cattle die and kinsmen die, and so one dies oneself; but the fame of a dead man's deeds never dies - and that is the one thing that never dies. All doorways before you go in should be spied out, all openings peered into: for it cannot be known where foes sit in the hall ahead. Hear, Loddfafnir, and take the counsel: rise not at night save to serve or to guard; better unbidden than over-bidden? - the injunctions run to weapon-craft and wife-craft, the north's etiquette as commandment.",
