    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "An apple cast in the queen's lap was the sign of the great child; Volsung's hall was built around it, and from the apple came Sigurd's line - the ancestry-token of the god's own gift. The saga ran the whole arc: the wolf-cloak vengeance, the sword Gram reforged, the dragon's slaying and the birds, Brynhild's waking and the oath, the betrayal in bed, Gudrun's feast of vengeance, and the last sons stoned - all as Gripir had foretold.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Volsunga saga chs. 1-2 (Morris & Magnusson 1870); not verbatim. / Paraphrase-synthesis of Volsunga saga chs. 1-44 (Morris & Magnusson 1870); not verbatim."
      }
    ]
