        id: "1",
        text: "The witnesses compared: Voluspa's givers are Odin, Hoenir and Lodurr; Snorri's are Odin, Vili and Ve; the gifts divide as breath-mind-colour or as life-wit-speech - the doctrine stable, the inventory fluid. The first-humans motif collected across its witnesses: Voluspa's shore-walk (three gods, two trees, three gifts: breath, mind, colour), Snorri's systematization (Odin, Vili, Ve; life, wit, and speech-senses), Lokasenna's stray notices (the gods' shore-walk as a stock tale quoted in the flyting), and the name-lore (askr, ash; embla, elm or vine, on the disputed reading).",
        note: "Paraphrase-synthesis of the variant-traditions; not verbatim."
