    canonical_translation: "Brodeur 1916 (public domain); Bellows 1923 (public domain)",
    narrative: {
      en: "The elemental-file holds the fire-ice motif's witnesses. The creation-polarity: Niflheim's eleven venom-rivers freezing into rime at the gap's north rim, Muspell's fire-world fenced with flame at the south, and the thaw quickening Ymir in between (the record norse-ginnungagap-void holds the meeting) - the elements are not abstractions but countries, each with named geography and population (the frost-giants' realm; Muspell's sons, Surtr their captain).\n\nThe persisting offices: the fire-side holds the end's office (Surtr with the flaming sword 'at? - 'the? - 'world's? - rim? - 'since? - 'the? - 'beginning? - the record norse-ragnarok-battles holds the final burning; the riders of Muspell crossing Bifrost - the record norse-bifrost-gjallarhorn's scheduled demolition); the ice-side holds the underworld's office (the venom-rivers of Hel's realm - the record norse-hel-realm; the corpse-spring Hvergelmir; the Fimbulwinter as the doom's own ice - the record norse-fimbulwinter-wolves). The motif's proverb-form: the lore summarized as 'the? - 'world? - 'lives? - 'between? - fire? - 'and? - ice? - 'and? - 'ends? - in? - fire? - 'after? - 'ice? - - the elemental bookends doctrine.\n\nThe record's cultural functions are the elemental-geography doctrine (the elements as populated countries with named captains - the north's own climate-theology: winter as an inhabitable realm) and the bookend-doctrine (the cosmos bracketed by its two elements: born of their meeting, ended by the fire's return, renewed between them). And the skaldic kennings complete the file: the elemental diction (fire as 'Muspell's? - flame? - 'and? - 'the? - ice? - as? - 'the? - 'venom-rivers? - 'cold) evidencing the motif's poetic currency. In the atlas, the record anchors the elemental-creation family: each a tradition's element-pair behind creation; the Norse one is distinctive in the populated elements and the bookend-structure.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the void-record, the Surtr-material and the Fimbulwinter-record: here the motif runs whole.\n\nThe record's climate-theology completes the file: the elements as the north's lived experience (the winter's inhabitable country, the fire's hearth-edge) - the cosmic polarity read from the farm-year's own bookends, creation-theology as climate-observation. And the renewal-clause completes it: the new age's restored shield-regime (the record norse-svalinn-shield) - the elements' bookend-structure closing with a managed sun, the motif's happy ending engineered. The record's place-lore completes the file: the elemental names carried into geography (the Muspell-word's Germanic reach beyond Scandinavia, the frost-names of the northern coasts) - the elements' polarity documented in toponymy, the creation's bookends readable on the map."
    },
