    summary: {
      en: "Freyja's sei\xF0r-office collected: the introduction-clause (Ynglinga saga: the Vanir hostage teaching the Aesir the magic they did not have), Odin's apprenticeship (the god learning the witchcraft 'that? - 'was? - 'thought? - unmanly? - - the ergi-cost documented in the same chapter), the flyting's charge (Loki accusing the goddess of promiscuity-magic: 'thou? - 'didst? - 'ride? - 'and? - 'love? - 'many? - 'a? - man? - in? - witch-shape? -), and the late moralization (Sorla thattr: the necklace-bargain and the war-curse). The record is the sei\xF0r-mistress file: the goddess as the magic-system's teacher and its social hazard.",
      zh: "\u8299\u857E\u96C5\u8CFD\u5FB7\u8077\u80FD\u7684\u5168\u96C6\uFF1A\u50B3\u5165\u689D\u6B3E\uFF08\u300A\u5C24\u6069\u683C\u6797\u52A0\u85A9\u8FE6\u300B\uFF1A\u83EF\u7D0D\u4EBA\u8CEA\u5411\u963F\u85A9\u795E\u65CF\u50B3\u6388\u4ED6\u5011\u672A\u66FE\u64C1\u6709\u7684\u9B54\u6CD5\uFF09\u3001\u5967\u4E01\u7684\u5B78\u5F92\u8EAB\u4EFD\uFF08\u795E\u660E\u7FD2\u5F97\u9019\u300C\u88AB\u8996\u70BA\u4E0D\u7537\u4E0D\u5973\u300D\u7684\u5DEB\u8853\u2014\u2014\u540C\u4E00\u7AE0\u7BC0\u8A18\u8F09\u4E86 ergi \u4E4B\u4EE3\u50F9\uFF09\u3001\u5435\u7F75\u4E2D\u7684\u6307\u63A7\uFF08\u6D1B\u57FA\u65A5\u8CAC\u5973\u795E\u4EE5\u5DEB\u8853\u4E4B\u5F62\u300C\u9A0E\u4E58\u4E26\u611B\u6200\u773E\u591A\u7537\u5B50\u300D\uFF09\uFF0C\u4EE5\u53CA\u665A\u671F\u7684\u9053\u5FB7\u5316\u6539\u5BEB\uFF08\u300A\u7D22\u723E\u62C9\u77ED\u7BC7\u300B\uFF1A\u9805\u93C8\u4EA4\u6613\u8207\u6230\u722D\u8A5B\u5492\uFF09\u3002\u6B64\u8A18\u9304\u662F\u8CFD\u5FB7\u5973\u5E2B\u6A94\u6848\uFF1A\u65E2\u662F\u9B54\u6CD5\u9AD4\u7CFB\u7684\u6559\u5E2B\uFF0C\u4E5F\u662F\u5176\u793E\u6703\u98A8\u96AA\u3002"
    },
    language: "Old Norse / Old Icelandic",
    canonical_translation: "Laing 1844 (public domain); Bellows 1923 (public domain)",
    narrative: {
      en: "The sei\xF0r-mistress file holds Freyja's magic-office. The introduction-clause: at the Aesir-Vanir peace, the hostage-goddess brought the north's magic - 'Freyja? - 'taught? - the? - Aesir? - sei\xF0r? - 'as? - 'it? - 'was? - 'practiced? - among? - the? - Vanir? - (Ynglinga's clause; the record norse-seidr-gullveig-expanded holds the practice-file) - the goddess as the pantheon's magic-teacher: the Aesir's power-set (thunder, law, runes) completed by the Vanir import (prophecy, love-craft, spirit-riding).\n\nOdin's apprenticeship is the file's central paradox: the same chapter documents the god learning the art 'with? - 'the? - 'shame? - 'attached? - (the ergi-cost: sei\xF0r unmanns its male performer - the record's taboo-doctrine), so the chief-god's magic is a licensed transgression: the king of the gods practicing the women's art under the women's stigma. And the flyting's charge completes the hazard-register: Loki's accusation ('thou? - 'didst? - 'ride? - 'in? - witch-shape? - 'and? - 'love? - 'man? - after? - man? - - the sei\xF0r-flight as promiscuity: the goddess's magic and her loves charged in one breath), the social hazard that the practice-file's law-clauses codify.\n\nThe late moralization completes the file: Sorla thattr's re-narration (the necklace bought at the dwarfs' price, Odin's war-curse - the record norse-freyja-brisingamen holds the theft-and-duel register) - the converted era's moralization of the magic-goddess: love-craft as war's engine, the sei\xF0r-mistress domesticated into a cautionary tale. The record's cultural functions are the teacher-goddess doctrine (the pantheon's magic imported by a woman hostage - the Vanir culture-transfer as the gods' second education) and the hazard-doctrine (the magic's gender-stigma documented from Odin's apprenticeship to the law-codes' clauses). In the atlas, the record anchors the initiate-goddess family: each a tradition's goddess of magic as teacher; Freyja is distinctive in the ergi-cost her students pay.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the sei\xF0r-practice-record, the necklace-record and the Gullveig-record: here the goddess's office runs whole.\n\nThe record's institutional reach completes the file: the sei\xF0r-mistress's office documented across the pantheon's history (the Vanir import at the treaty, Odin's apprenticeship, the flyting's charge, the converted era's moralization) - the goddess's magic-office as the corpus's longest-running institution-story. And the ergi-economics completes it: the magic's gender-cost paid by its male students - the teacher's art priced in stigma, the system's gender-grammar visible in every transaction. The record's cat-chariot register completes the file: the goddess's transport documented (the two cats drawing her chariot - the travel-magic beside the sei\xF0r-office) - the sei\xF0r-mistress's mobility and her magic one household-economy, the goddess's daily apparatus listed with her rites."
    },
