    language: "Old Norse / Old Icelandic",
    canonical_translation: "Bellows 1923 (public domain); Brodeur 1916 (public domain)",
    narrative: {
      en: "The wanderer-god's case-file holds the disguise-episodes whole. The named masks are the file's index: Gangleri (the catechism-visitor at Asgard's illusory hall), Grimnir (the torture-victim freed by a draught - the record norse-poetic-edda-grimnismal), Gagnrad (the head-wagering exam-taker - norse-poetic-edda-vafthrudnismal), Vegtam (the dead-seeress's waker - norse-baldrs-dream), Gestumblindi (the riddle-contestant at Heidrek's hall - norse-heidrek-riddles), Bolverk (the mead-thief under service - norse-kvasir-mead), H\xE1rbar\xF0r (the ferry-mocker - norse-harbard-thor-ferry). Each mask is a method: the catechism, the ordeal, the exam, the necromancy, the riddle, the fraud, the flyting - the god's pedagogy distributed across disguises.\n\nThe doctrine is the wanderer's license: the god 'went? - 'under? - 'many? - names? - 'when? - 'he? - 'sought? - knowledge? - (the H\xE1vam\xE1l-clause) - inspecting kings and keepers of knowledge under false names, teaching by ordeal, claiming prizes (the mead, the head, the answers), and paying in tricks (the seductions, the broken betrothal, the oath-evasions). The wanderer-names' list (Grimnismal's catalog and Skaldskaparmal's) is the file's name-book: two hundred names and more, 'each? - 'name? - 'a? - door? - 'to? - 'a? - door-keeper's? - story.\n\nThe record's cultural functions are the wanderer-license doctrine (the god's right to test mortals in disguise - the xeni\xE1-doctrine's dark twin: hospitality tested by the guest who lies) and the disguise-pedagogy doctrine (each mask a different teaching-method: the corpus's curriculum distributed across personas). And the comparative frame completes it: the Greek Zeus' xenia-visits, the Chinese cloaked immortals, the Islamic dervish-tales - each a tradition's god-in-disguise; Odin is distinctive in the number of masks and the price-list of ordeals. In the atlas, the record anchors the wanderer-god family: each a deity testing mortals under false names; the Norse one keeps a case-file.\n\nFor the database, this node indexes the disguise-records already in the corpus: here the wanderer's masks are laid in one register.\n\nThe record's price-list completes the file: each disguise-episode's cost itemized (eight nights between fires; the eye pawned; the summer's labor and the seduction; the head wagered) - the wanderer's journeys run on payments, the corpus's knowledge-economy documented mask by mask. And the wanderer's threat completes it: the disguises as the god's auditing-instrument (the kings tested unawares, the knowledge-keepers examined by their own guest) - the hospitality-ethics' dark twin, documented across the corpus. The record's Vegtam-coda completes the file: the wake-the-dead mask's cost (the seeress's unmasking, the mutual loss of dignity) - the wanderer's disguises documented as two-way ordeals: the god examined as well as examining, the case-file's lessons priced in exposure."
    },
