    language: "Old Norse / Old Icelandic",
    canonical_translation: "Brodeur 1916 (public domain); Bellows 1923 (public domain)",
    narrative: {
      en: "The kin-symbol file holds Sif's hair in its symbolic frames. The episode (norse-mjolnir-forging holds the forge): Loki's midnight shearing of Thor's wife - the trick that opens the treasure-cycle - and the dwarf-gift: hair of real gold that 'grows? - 'like? - 'other? - hair? - - the honor restored in metal. The kenning-economy: 'Sif's? - hair? - is? - a? - standard? - gold-kenning? - (the Skaldskaparmal lists) - the wife's honor priced in metal: the insult measured in gold, the restoration paid in the same coin - the household's economy in verse-diction.\n\nThe crop-reading is the file's interpretive register: the scholars' argument that the golden hair is grain - the field's harvest as the earth-wife's hair, the cutting and regrowth as the agricultural year - 'hair? - 'like? - 'the? - corn? - 'cut? - 'and? - 'grown? - again? - (the fertility-reading built from the kenning-lists, where Sif's hair names gold AND the golden crop is named by the same figure). The household-frame completes it: Sif as Thor's wife (the thunderer married to the earth-figure: rain married to field), mother of Ullr (the ski-god, stepson) and Thrud (the strength-daughter) - the thunder-household's roster.\n\nAnd the flyting's charge: Loki's taunt at the feast ('I? - 'know? - 'one? - who? - shared? - thy? - bed? - 'the? - adultery-charge - the record norse-lokasenna-flyting) - the kin-symbol under moral attack, the honor-theme continued after the hair is restored. The record's cultural functions are the honor-economy doctrine (the wife's hair as the household's visible worth, priced and paid in gold) and the crop-symbolism doctrine (the golden harvest on the field-wife's head - the fertility-reading documented in the kennings). In the atlas, the record anchors the kin-symbol family: each a tradition's household-emblem read symbolically; Sif's is distinctive in the kenning-economy.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the forge-record and the flyting-record: here the symbolism runs whole.\n\nThe record's iconographic reach completes the file: the golden-haired goddess documented in no surviving image but reconstructed from the kennings - the kin-symbol's evidence entirely poetic, which is itself the datum (Sif's office documented by the verse-economy alone). And the flyting's continuation completes it: the honor-theme running after the restoration - the corpus's longest portrait of a household-insult and its repair, from shearing to hearing? - hearing? - to flyting.\n\n The record's harvest-parallel completes the file: the kenning-economy\u2019s double entry (gold as Sif\u2019s hair; grain as the field\u2019s gold) - the household\u2019s wealth and the field\u2019s wealth named by one figure, the kin-symbol\u2019s two economies fused in a single diction."
    },
