    license: "Public domain (Brodeur 1916; Bellows 1923); passages below are labeled paraphrases",
    summary: {
      en: "The treaty-marriage's ritual grammar expanded: the atonement-frame (the armed arrival, the compensations: husband-choice, laugh-payment, star-setting - each a legal form), the feet-choice's ritual logic (the bride's consent manufactured by ceremony: the choice by proxy), the cohabitation-clause (nine nights alternating - the experimental marriage as contract term), the dissolution and its aftermath (the return to Thrymheim, the ski-goddess's continuing visits: 'she? - 'comes? - 'to? - 'the? - feasts? - still? - the treaty's persistence), and the flyting's scandal-clause (Loki's charge of the goddess's bed-visit to her father's? - the? - incest-insinuation). The record is the treaty-marriage file.",
      zh: "\u689D\u7D04\u5A5A\u59FB\u7684\u5100\u5F0F\u8A9E\u6CD5\u64F4\u8B80\uFF1A\u8CE0\u511F\u6846\u67B6\uFF08\u6301\u68B0\u800C\u4F86\uFF1B\u88DC\u511F\u4E09\u9805\u2014\u2014\u64C7\u592B\u3001\u9017\u7B11\u3001\u7F6E\u661F\u2014\u2014\u5404\u81EA\u7686\u70BA\u6CD5\u5F8B\u5F62\u5F0F\uFF09\u3001\u8DB3\u9078\u7684\u5100\u5F0F\u908F\u8F2F\uFF08\u4EE5\u4EE3\u9078\u88FD\u9020\u65B0\u5A18\u540C\u610F\uFF09\u3001\u540C\u4F4F\u689D\u6B3E\uFF08\u5404\u65BC\u5C0D\u65B9\u5BB6\u4E2D\u4E5D\u591C\u2014\u2014\u4EE5\u5951\u7D04\u689D\u6B3E\u5448\u73FE\u7684\u5BE6\u9A57\u5A5A\u59FB\uFF09\u3001\u89E3\u9AD4\u53CA\u5176\u5F8C\u7E8C\uFF08\u8FD4\u56DE\u7279\u5442\u59C6\u6D77\u59C6\uFF1B\u6ED1\u96EA\u5973\u795E\u4ECD\u6642\u5E38\u8D74\u5BB4\u2014\u2014\u689D\u7D04\u4E4B\u5EF6\u7E8C\uFF09\uFF0C\u4EE5\u53CA\u5435\u7F75\u4E2D\u7684\u919C\u805E\u689D\u6B3E\uFF08\u6D1B\u57FA\u6697\u793A\u5979\u8207\u7236\u89AA\u540C\u5E8A\u4E4B\u4E82\u502B\u6307\u63A7\uFF09\u3002\u6B64\u8A18\u9304\u662F\u689D\u7D04\u5A5A\u59FB\u6A94\u6848\u3002"
    },
    language: "Old Norse / Old Icelandic",
    canonical_translation: "Brodeur 1916 (public domain); Bellows 1923 (public domain)",
    narrative: {
      en: "The treaty-marriage file expands the ritual grammar of Njord and Ska\xF0i (norse-njord-skadi holds the core narrative). The compensations as legal forms: the husband-choice by feet (the bride's consent manufactured by proxy - the ceremony choosing for her), the laugh-payment (Loki's goat-trick: the settlement's mirth-clause, legally owed), and the star-setting (the father's eyes as memorial - the compensation's permanent form). Each compensation is a recognized legal instrument (choice, satisfaction, memorial) staged in myth.\n\nThe cohabitation-clause and its aftermath: the nine-nights-alternating term ('the? - 'experimental? - 'marriage: 'each? - 'dwelling? - nine? - nights? - 'in? - the? - other's? - home) as a contract's trial-period; the dissolution on evidence (the gull-cries and wolf-howls as the experiment's data); and the treaty's persistence: the divorce does not end the alliance - 'Ska\xF0i? - 'comes? - 'to? - 'the? - feasts? - 'still? - (the prose's clause: the ex-wife attending the gods' assemblies, the treaty-hospitality continuing), the winter-goddess keeping her seat in the pantheon after the marriage ends.\n\nAnd the flyting's scandal-clause: Loki's charge ('thou? - 'didst? - share? - thy? - bed? - 'with? - thy? - brother? - - the incest-insinuation aimed at Ska\xF0i's giant-household: the treaty-union defamed by the trickster's charge), the marriage's honor under attack in the same genre that documents it. The record's cultural functions are the marriage-as-treaty doctrine (the divorce as a treaty's normal dissolution, the alliance persisting past the marriage - the north's own politics-of-marriage) and the compensation-grammar doctrine (choice, laugh, memorial as legal instruments staged in myth). In the atlas, the record anchors the treaty-marriage family: each a union resolving a feud; the Norse one is distinctive in the trial-term and the surviving alliance.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the core-record and the Skadi-cult-materials: here the ritual grammar runs whole.\n\nThe record's ritual-theory completes the file: the compensations' grammar (choice, laugh, memorial) documented as the north's standard settlement-instruments (the same three payments the sagas' feud-settlements use), so the mythic marriage documents the legal marriage's machinery - the treaty-union as the north's own divorce-law in miniature. And the ski-goddess's continuing cult completes it: Ska\xF0i's winter-places and snowshoe-place-names - the treaty's residue written into the landscape.\n\n The record's winter-office completes the file: Ska\xF0i's continuing functions after the divorce (the ski-hunts, the mountain-hall)s keeping, the feasts) seat) documented as the treaty)s standing army of rights - the ex-wife)s privileges itemized, the north)s own post-settlement law in mythic dress. And the parallel-settlement register completes it: the sagas) real divorce-and-settlement cases (the property-divisions and the feast-rights negotiated) - the mythic treaty)s grammar documented in the courts) practice."
    },
