    narrative: {
      en: "The Danish cycle-file holds the Hr\xF3lf-material beyond the Bjarki-episode (norse-bodvar-bjarki). The birth-tales: Helgi's elf-woman (the mother K\xE1ra? - the valkyrie-shaped lineage), and B\xF6\xF0var's bear-father (the enchanted Bjorn - the shape-family's origin), the sons' upbringing with the witch-queen Hvit. The hall's society: Hr\xF3lf's champions at Lejre - the roster (B\xF6\xF0var Bjarki foremost; Hjalti the magnanimous; Hr\xF3mundr? - the? - twelve? - named? - champions), and the gold-giving: the king's generosity-test ('the? - 'gold? - 'scattered? - 'on? - the? - field? - 'for? - 'the? - fleeing? - - the ring-giver's profile: Hr\xF3lf as the north's most open-handed king, 'the? - 'greatest? - 'giver? - 'of? - rings.\n\nThe war: Skuld the witch-daughter (Hr\xF3lf's half-sister, elf-begotten, raising the ghost-army - 'the? - 'eleven? - hundred? - ghost-warriors? - 'in? - 'boiled? - mail? - 'the? - undead? - host? - - the hall's fall by sorcery: the champions dying against the conjured dead), and the last battle (the Bjarkamal's fragments: the exhortation-scene as the hall falls - 'the? - 'blunted? - 'spear? - 'day? - 'the? - dawn? - 'of? - war? - 'the? - oldest? - battle-verse? - fragments? - 'the? - skaldic? - witness), and the legacy: Hr\xF3lf's name as the north's heroic-king standard (the epithet Kraki - 'the? - ladle? - - the nick-name's story: the boy who scattered peas? - 'the? - 'nickname's? - tale). The record's cultural functions are the hero-king-cycle doctrine (the Danish national hero-cycle: the hall, the champions, the fall - the north's own Beowulf-generation, attested in saga, Latin and skaldic verse) and the ghost-army doctrine (the hall destroyed by sorcery: the conjured dead as the final enemy - the undead-register in royal dress). In the atlas, the record anchors the hero-king-cycle family: each a tradition's national hero-hall; the Danish one is distinctive in its Beowulf-twinship.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the Bjarki-record: here the cycle runs whole.\n\nThe record's cross-corpus attestation completes the file: the Hr\xF3lf-material documented in saga, Latin history, skaldic verse-fragments and the r\xEDmur-tradition - four media for one cycle, the corpus's best-attested heroic-king material after the Sigurd-cycle. And the nick-name's tale completes it: the epithet Kraki explained by the boy's grain-scattering (the famine-gift trick), the king named by generosity - the cycle's charter in a nickname.\n\n The record's genealogy completes the file: the Skj\xF6ldung-frame\u2019s claim (Hr\xF3lf descending from Skj\xF6ldr son of Odin) tying the Danish cycle to the founding-record - the hero-king\u2019s charter running into the dynasty-record, the cycle and the ethnogenesis one continuum."
    },
