    license: "Public domain (Rafn 1829); passages below are labeled paraphrases",
    summary: {
      en: "The \xDEorsteinn-file: the Viking's-son saga (the hero descending to? - the? - descent? - 'to? - Permsland? - 'the? - giant-king's? - courts? - - the quest into the giant-lands; the drum? - the? - 'magic? - drum? - 'that? - 'carries? - the? - heroes? - over? - the? - sea), the Giantland-court adventures (the giant-king's? - the? - feats? - - the strength-contests, the rescue of the? - princesses), and the B\xE6jarmagn-th\xE1ttr (the little hero? - the? - 'pocket-sized? - champion? - 'in? - the? - giants'? - courts? - - the size-inversion comedy: the man-champion among giants). The record is the quasi-legendary file: the family-sagas' heroic cousin.",
      zh: "\u7D22\u723E\u65AF\u6CF0\u56E0\u6A94\u6848\uFF1A\u7DAD\u4EAC\u4E4B\u5B50\u85A9\u8FE6\uFF08\u82F1\u96C4\u6DF1\u5165\u4F69\u723E\u59C6\u862D\u5DE8\u4EBA\u4E4B\u5730\uFF1B\u9B54\u6CD5\u4E4B\u9F13\u8F09\u82F1\u96C4\u8D8A\u6D77\uFF09\u3001\u5DE8\u4EBA\u570B\u5BAE\u5EF7\u5192\u96AA\uFF08\u529B\u91CF\u7AF6\u8CFD\u3001\u71DF\u6551\u516C\u4E3B\uFF09\uFF0C\u4EE5\u53CA\u300A\u8C9D\u96C5\u99AC\u683C\u5C3C\u77ED\u7BC7\u300B\uFF08\u300C\u8896\u73CD\u52C7\u58EB\u300D\u8EAB\u9677\u5DE8\u4EBA\u5BAE\u5EF7\u2014\u2014\u5C3A\u5BF8\u5012\u932F\u7684\u559C\u5287\uFF1A\u5E38\u4EBA\u8EAB\u91CF\u5C0D\u6C7A\u5DE8\u4EBA\uFF09\u3002\u6B64\u8A18\u9304\u662F\u6E96\u50B3\u8AAA\u6A94\u6848\uFF1A\u5BB6\u65CF\u85A9\u8FE6\u7684\u82F1\u96C4\u5802\u5144\u5F1F\u3002"
    },
    language: "Old Norse / Old Icelandic",
    canonical_translation: "Fornaldar sogur nordrlanda ed. C. C. Rafn, Copenhagen 1829 (public domain); paraphrase",
    narrative: {
      en: "The quasi-legendary file holds the \xDEorsteinn-register. The Viking's-son saga: the descent-quest (the hero sailing to Permsland, the giant-king's courts - the giant-lands' geography as the quest's stage), the magic-drum (the drum that carries the heroes over the sea? - 'the? - 'drum? - 'of? - the? - giant's? - daughter? - 'that? - 'crosses? - the? - water? - - the corpus's sound-vehicle: travel by drumbeat), and the strength-contests and rescues (the giant-court's trials: the princesses freed, the feasts survived - the quest-saga's standard machinery in the giant-register).\n\nThe B\xE6jarmagn-th\xE1ttr: the size-inversion comedy (the little champion pocket-sized among giants - the? - 'the? - 'man-sized? - hero? - 'in? - the? - giants'? - hall? - 'the? - furniture? - 'too? - large? - - the hero living in the giants' oversized world: the bed, the horn, the - the comedy of scale), and the trickster-feats (the little hero outwitting the giants at their own feast - the David-register in Norse dress). The record's cultural functions are the giant-land-quest doctrine (the giant-lands as the quest's geography: courts, feasts and trials across the border) and the scale-inversion doctrine (the size-comedy as heroism's register: the small champion among the large). In the atlas, the record anchors the quasi-legendary family: each a tradition's heroic-saga cousin-mode; the Norse one is distinctive in the drum-vehicle.\n\nFor the database, this node extends the heroic file's giant-land mode: the courts, the drum, the pocket-champion.\n\nThe record's mythic register completes the file: the quasi-legendary sagas' giant-lands are the eddic Jotunheim's domesticated version (the courts and feasts modeled on human halls), so the heroic-cousin mode documents the myth-world's borderlands as habitable country - the giants as hosts, judges and kin. And the sagas' transmission completes it: the \xDEorsteinn-material's circulation in the r\xEDmur-tradition - the quasi-legendary file's medieval afterlife.\n\n The record's giant-court protocol completes the file: the giants) halls run on human etiquette (the guest-rights, the feast-seats, the contests of strength as courtly games) - the myth-world)s borderlands documented as diplomatic territory, the quest)s trials a courtier)s ordeal. And the saga)s settlement-epilogue completes it: the hero)s return and the family)s founding-register - the giant-land)s exploits converted into Iceland)s settlement-genealogies, the quest)s prize a farmstead.\n\n The record's kinship-web completes the file: the saga)s ties to the greater cycles (J\xF6kull the outlaw-father figure; the V\xE9steinn? - the friendship-oath register shared with the Egil-material) - the quasi-legendary mode as the heroic corpus)s connective tissue, its heroes crossing into the family-sagas) genealogies. And the giant-king)s court-drama completes it: the wisdom-contests and gift-negotiations at the giant-feasts - the quest)s trials as diplomacy, the borderland)s court-life documented."
    },
