    language: "Old Norse / Old Icelandic",
    canonical_translation: "Palsson & Edwards, Gautrek's Saga, London 1970 (paraphrased); Fornaldar sogur ed. Rafn 1829 (public domain)",
    narrative: {
      en: "The alternate-founding file holds Gautreks saga's charter-tales (norse-starkadr-gautreks holds the Vikar-chapter). Gauti's madness: the king riding north after his hawk till the cliff-edge - the founding-madness: the kingdom begun by a king lost to the chase, who rode into the unknown. The cliff-kingdom's law: the family-cult of the rock (the elders sent over the cliff when the milk ran short - the sacrifice-law that bought the cows' milk: the household's economy as a cult of the crag, the corpus's blackest founding-institution).\n\nGautrekr's founding: the son's restoration of the line (the mad king's heir founding the Gautar-dynasty properly - the lineage-record of the West-Gautar kings), and the frame-tales complete the file: Starkadr's youth-tales inside the same Gautar-world, and Ref's gift-economy (the trickster-carpenter whose gifts ascend the chain from king to emperor - the saga's own satire on gift-economics, each gift's profit calculated).\n\nThe record's cultural functions are the alternate-genealogy doctrine (the Gautar-line as Sweden's second royal house: the founding told in madness where the Ynglinga told it in migration) and the founding-sacrifice doctrine (the cliff-law as the founding's dark institution: the elders' deaths buying the herd's milk). In the atlas, the record anchors the alternate-founding family: each a tradition's second charter; the Gautar one is distinctive in the madness-frame.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the Starkadr-record and the Ynglinga-record: here the alternate charter-file.\n\nThe record's genre-completes the doctrine: Gautreks saga's frame-tale structure (the comic-dark founding-tales nested inside the champion's biography) is the fornaldarsaga's anthology-mode - several founding-styles in one document: the madness-charter, the sacrifice-law, the gift-economy satire and the hero-tale, each a different institution's origin told in the same frame. And the saga's reception completes it: the Gautar-line's claim echoed in the Swedish royal genealogies - the alternate charter's reach into the historical dynasties.\n\n The record's Starkadr-junction completes the file: the champion)s biography embedded in the same saga-frame (the Gautar-world shared), so the alternate-charter document doubles as the great champion)s home-context - the founding-tales and the hero-tale one document. And the saga)s black-humor register completes it: the cliff-law and the madness-ride told without horror - the founding)s institutions narrated in the saga-mode)s deadpan, the corpus)s most ironized charter.\n\n The record's saga-sequence completes the file: the frame)s nested tales (the madness-charter, the sacrifice-law, the Star-cad youth, Ref)s chain and Gautrekr)s marriage-quest) read in sequence as the fornaldarsaga)s anthology - one document sampling four founding-genres, the corpus)s most composite charter-text. And the Gautar-kingdom)s geography completes it: the West-Gautland sites (the cliff, the farms, the market-ways) carrying the saga)s institutions into the modern landscape - the alternate charter)s geography documented."
    },
