    canonical_translation: "Bellows 1923 (public domain); Brodeur 1916 (public domain)",
    narrative: {
      en: "The fire-giant's stray-file holds Surtr's notices beyond the battle (norse-ragnarok-battles holds the duel; norse-primordial-fire-ice the elemental frame). The creation-placement: the guard at the rim 'from? - 'the? - first? - (Snorri's clause: Surtr 'sits? - 'at? - 'the? - world's? - end? - 'guarded? - 'by? - fire? - - the fire-world's warden since creation: the doom's captain already posted at the beginning - the eschatology's geography built into the cosmogony).\n\nThe name-lore and the flyting's claim: Surtr's title ('the? - 'black? - one? - 'the? - soot-giant's? - name? - - the fire named by its residue), and Loki's own fire-credentials ('I? - 'was? - 'inside? - 'the? - 'the? - - the flyting's boast: the trickster claiming to have seen the fire-folk's ships and weapons - Loki as the doom's travel-agent, the record norse-lokasenna-flyting's charge). And the continental witness: the Old High German Muspilli (the 9th-century doom-poem's fire-judgment verse - the word documented outside Scandinavia), and the placement-debate: Muspell as native Germanic eschatology or Christian-era import (the scholars' fire-lore argument: the doctrine's age as the record's open question).\n\nThe record's cultural functions are the fire-warden doctrine (the doom's captain posted from creation: the end's geography built into the beginning) and the name-reach doctrine (the Muspell-word's continental circulation - the fire-world's name as the north's shared Germanic eschatological vocabulary). In the atlas, the record anchors the fire-warden family: each a tradition's doom-guardian; Surtr is distinctive in the creation-day posting.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the battle-record and the elemental-file: here the fire-giant's strays.\n\nThe record's Icelandic geography completes the file: the fire-world's modern names (the volcano-fields and lava-coasts of the island as Muspell's visible residue - the settlers' own volcanic evidence behind the doctrine: Iceland's eruptions as the fire-world's recurring news), so the stray-file's doctrine is grounded in the landscape the corpus was written in: the fire-giant's realm documented in the authors' own backyard. And the source-criticism completes the file: the Muspell-material's manuscript distribution (the word appearing in Snorri and the eddic fragments but thinly in the skaldic corpus) - the fire-lore's evidence-pattern documented as the debate's basis.\n\nThe file's placement-argument completes the register: the two readings' evidence weighed (the V\xF6lusp\xE1's own fire-imagery argued native by the eddic scholars; the Muspilli-parallel argued import by the philologists - the debate's method documented: word-history against poem-structure), so the stray-file's open question is itself the datum: the corpus's eschatology dated by an argument still running. And the Loki-fire link completes it: the trickster's kinship with the fire-world (the record norse-loki-genealogy's brood and Loki's own flight as an eagle of flame-adjacent shape) - the fire-giant's file tied to the trickster's biography."
    },
