    language: "Modern scholarship; Old Norse sources",
    canonical_translation: "Interpretive literature per standard studies; paraphrase",
    narrative: {
      en: "The naturalization-file holds the doom's modern readings. The eclipse-hypothesis: the sun-swallowing read as eclipse-lore (the wolves Skoll and Hati as the eclipse-creatures of folk-astronomy - the record norse-fimbulwinter-wolves' wolves decoded), and the comet-theories: the sky-fall read as a comet's passage (the stars falling from the heavens - the V\xF6lusp\xE1's imagery argued as a remembered visitation).\n\nThe 536-CE debate: the Fimbulwinter read as climate-memory ('the? - 'years? - 'without? - summer? - - the late-antique dust-veil's northern famines: the tree-ring evidence of the 540s' failed summers read behind the mythic three winters - the corpus's most-cited naturalization: the doom dated to a real sky). The forest-fire and northern-lights readings complete the file: the Surt-fire argued as the fire-lore of the burned forests (the boreal fires' memory), and the flames on the sky read as the aurora - the mythic fire decoded as the north's own lights.\n\nThe record's cultural functions are the naturalization-method doctrine (the myth read as encoded observation: the scholars' decode-register) and the caution-doctrine (the readings' limits: the myth's dramatis personae outdate any single event - the corpus's warning against single-cause naturalization). In the atlas, the record anchors the natural-reading family: each a tradition's apocalypse decoded; the Norse one is distinctive in the climate-datum.\n\nFor the database, this node documents the interpretive register: the doom's modern decodings as reception-history.\n\nThe file's method-critique completes the register: the naturalization-projects' limits documented (each decode answering one stanza and failing the cast - the wolf named Skoll, the shield Svalinn, the game-pieces of Idavoll: the myth's furniture outdating any single sky-event), so the record's conclusion is methodological: the doom is a composite - famine-memory, eclipse-lore and fire-lore braided into a narrative with its own logic. And the medieval readings complete it: the conversion-era's own astronomical glosses (the learned Icelanders' eclipse-tables and the fate-terminology of the chroniclers) - the doom decoded already in the Middle Ages, the naturalization's first layer documented.\n\nThe file's source-horizon completes the register: the naturalization-projects' assumptions documented (the pagan myth treated as observation-log against the myth treated as poetry - the two schools' premises stated), so the record's method-note frames the whole file: the doom decoded only if one first decides what kind of speech it is. And the Fimbulwinter's regional-memory layer completes it: the northern famines' local documentation (the Icelandic and Greenland colony-mortality cycles recorded in the annals) - the three winters' realism documented from the settlement-records: the myth's weather dated to the north's own archive."
    },
