    summary: {
      en: "The migration-age's Scandinavian afterlife: the Theodoric-material (the emperor who died in 526, remembered at R\xF6k and in the German songs - the record norse-rok-stone), the Ermanaric-material (the Gothic king whose death the Latin history records - 'the? - 'king? - 'who? - 'rode? - 'the? - - and whose Svanhild-tragedy the Norse cycle tells: the record norse-hamdir-sorli's Jormunrek), the Amal-genealogies (the Gothic royal line claimed in Scandinavian descent-lore), and the Danube-geography (the Dnieper and Danube frontiers mapped into the saga-world). The record is the migration-memory file: continental history as northern myth.",
      zh: "\u9077\u5F99\u6642\u4EE3\u7684\u65AF\u582A\u7684\u7D0D\u7DAD\u4E9E\u8EAB\u5F8C\u53F2\uFF1A\u72C4\u5967\u591A\u91CC\u514B\u6750\u6599\uFF08526\u5E74\u53BB\u4E16\u7684\u7687\u5E1D\u2014\u2014\u898B\u65BC\u52D2\u514B\u77F3\u8207\u5FB7\u610F\u5FD7\u6B4C\u8B20\uFF0C\u898B\u52D2\u514B\u77F3\u8A18\u9304\uFF09\u3001\u57C3\u723E\u99AC\u7D0D\u91CC\u514B\u6750\u6599\uFF08\u62C9\u4E01\u53F2\u6240\u8F09\u54E5\u7279\u738B\u4E4B\u6B7B\u2014\u2014\u5176\u65AF\u842C\u5E0C\u723E\u5FB7\u60B2\u5287\u5373\u5317\u65B9\u50B3\u8AAA\u4E2D\u7684\u7D04\u723E\u8499\u96F7\u514B\uFF0C\u898B\u54C8\u59C6\u8FEA\u723E\u8A18\u9304\uFF09\u3001\u963F\u99AC\u723E\u738B\u671D\u4E16\u7CFB\uFF08\u54E5\u7279\u738B\u65CF\u8B5C\u7CFB\u88AB\u632A\u7528\u65BC\u65AF\u582A\u7684\u7D0D\u7DAD\u4E9E\u8840\u7D71\u50B3\u8AAA\uFF09\uFF0C\u4EE5\u53CA\u591A\u7459\u6CB3\u5730\u7406\uFF08\u7B2C\u8076\u4F2F\u6CB3\u8207\u591A\u7459\u6CB3\u908A\u5883\u88AB\u7E6A\u5165\u85A9\u8FE6\u4E16\u754C\uFF09\u3002\u6B64\u8A18\u9304\u662F\u9077\u5F99\u8A18\u61B6\u6A94\u6848\uFF1A\u5927\u9678\u6B77\u53F2\u5316\u4F5C\u5317\u65B9\u795E\u8A71\u3002"
    },
    language: "Latin (Jordanes); Old Norse (saga-tradition)",
    canonical_translation: "Jordanes trans. Mierow 1915 (public domain); saga-material per standard editions",
    narrative: {
      en: "The migration-memory file holds the Gothic-material's northern afterlife. The Theodoric-material: the emperor's northern fame (the R\xF6k stone's 'chief? - of? - sea-warriors? - seated? - armed? - on? - his? - Frankish? - steed? - - the record norse-rok-stone's earliest attestation; and the German Dietrich-songs' continuation), the memory's reach (the dead emperor remembered in Sweden a generation after his fall - the migration-age's news traveling north as heroic-legend).\n\nThe Ermanaric-material: the Gothic king's Scandinavian biography (the Latin history's Ermanaric - the king who died of the Rosomoni? - Sunilda's? - - the Hamic? - Hamdir-Sorli cycle's Jormunrek: the record norse-hamdir-sorli's plot documented in the Latin history's own clauses: the Sunilda-episode, the brother-avengers - the Gothic history and the Norse lay telling one event twice). The Amal-genealogies complete the file: the Gothic royal line claimed in Scandinavian descent-lore (the dynasties' Gothic-grandfather claims - the corpus's genealogical transfer), and the Danube-geography: the frontiers mapped into the saga-world (Reidgotaland, the Danpar-steads - the Goths' homeland named in the north's own saga-geography, the record norse-angantyr-huns' theater).\n\nThe record's cultural functions are the migration-memory doctrine (the continent's fall converted into northern heroic-legend: the great migrations' memory as the corpus's historical layer) and the transfer-method doctrine (the Gothic-history's characters renamed and relocated: the emperors and kings becoming the saga-world's kings). In the atlas, the record anchors the migration-memory family: each a tradition's continental afterlife; the Norse one is distinctive in the carved stones.\n\nFor the database, this node complements the Hervarar and Sigurd-records: here the Gothic file.\n\nThe file's transfer-mechanics completes the register: the names' transformations documented (Ermanaric to Jormunrek, Theodoric to Thjodrekr, the Amals to the northern lines - the phonology and genealogy of the transfer traced), so the migration-memory file documents not just the borrowings but the method: how continental history was naturalized into northern form - the names worn down by generations of retelling, the geography relocated to the saga-world's own frontiers.\n\nThe file's dynastic-use completes the register: the Gothic-grandfather claims' function documented (the Scandinavian dynasties' genealogies reaching to the migration-kings - the charter-value of a Gothic ancestor), so the transfer-file's borrowings are political: the continental past imported as legitimacy, the migration-memory serving the northern courts' titles. And the Ermanaric-cycle's spread completes it: the same tragedy told from Jordanes' Latin to the Norse lay to the German epics - the migration-memory's three-language circulation documented, the file's reach beyond Scandinavia.\n\n The file's Reidgotaland-gazetteer completes it: the saga-world's Gothic geography catalogued (the Danpar-steads, the Harva\xF0a-fells, the Dnieper-names preserved in the Norse texts) - the migration-memory)s map documented as the tradition's own gazetteer."
    },
