    summary: {
      en: "The late-medieval compendia's file: Tr\xF3jumanna saga (the Trojan War's Norse retelling: the classical epic translated into saga-prose), Breta s\xF6gur (Geoffrey's Historia regum Britanniae in Norse: the British kings' book), and Merl\xEDn\xFAssp\xE1 (Gunnlaugr Leifsson's verse translation of Merlin's prophecies in eddic metre - 'the? - 'prophecies? - 'sung? - 'in? - 'the? - old? - measure? - - the French prophecy translated into the North's prophetic form). The record is the learned-reception file: the imported prophecies read in the native genre.",
      zh: "\u665A\u671F\u4E2D\u4E16\u7D00\u5F59\u7DE8\u6A94\u6848\uFF1A\u300A\u7279\u6D1B\u4F0A\u85A9\u8FE6\u300B\uFF08\u4EE5\u85A9\u8FE6\u6563\u6587\u8F49\u8FF0\u7279\u6D1B\u4F0A\u6230\u722D\u2014\u2014\u53E4\u5178\u53F2\u8A69\u7684\u5317\u6B50\u5316\uFF09\u3001\u300A\u5E03\u5217\u5854\u5C3C\u4EBA\u4E4B\u66F8\u300B\uFF08\u5091\u5F17\u91CC\u7684\u300A\u4E0D\u5217\u985B\u8AF8\u738B\u53F2\u300B\u4E4B\u8AFE\u65AF\u8B6F\u672C\uFF09\uFF0C\u4EE5\u53CA\u300A\u6885\u6797\u9810\u8A00\u8A69\u300B\uFF08\u8CA2\u52DE\u683C\xB7\u840A\u592B\u677E\u4EE5\u57C3\u9054\u97FB\u5F8B\u8B6F\u5BEB\u7684\u6885\u6797\u9810\u8A00\u2014\u2014\u300C\u4EE5\u53E4\u9AD4\u97FB\u5F8B\u541F\u5531\u7684\u9810\u8A00\u300D\uFF1A\u6CD5\u862D\u897F\u9810\u8A00\u88AB\u8B6F\u5165\u5317\u65B9\u7684\u9810\u8A00\u6587\u9AD4\uFF09\u3002\u6B64\u8A18\u9304\u662F\u535A\u5B78\u63A5\u53D7\u6A94\u6848\uFF1A\u5916\u4F86\u9810\u8A00\u4EE5\u672C\u571F\u6587\u9AD4\u95B1\u8B80\u3002"
    },
    language: "Old Norse / Old Icelandic",
    canonical_translation: "Older editions (Hauksbok; learned-saga editions); paraphrase",
    narrative: {
      en: "The learned-reception file holds the imported-myth register. Tr\xF3jumanna saga: the classical epic in saga-prose (the Trojan War translated for the Norse courts - the Dares-Phrygius tradition's saga-form: the classical heroes made saga-kings), and Breta s\xF6gur: the British book in Norse (Geoffrey's Historia translated - the British kings' and Arthur's material entering the north's bookshelf).\n\nMerl\xEDn\xFAssp\xE1 completes the file: the prophecies translated into the native genre (Gunnlaugr Leifsson's verse rendering of the Prophetiae Merlini - 'the? - 'prophecies? - 'sung? - 'in? - 'the? - old? - measure? - - the imported prophecy wearing the eddic form: the sibyl-tradition (the record norse-voluspa-sibyl) meeting Merlin - the reception's mirror: the North's prophecy-genre used to carry the imported doom). The record's cultural functions are the learned-translation doctrine (the romances translated into saga-prose: the North's bookshelf internationalized) and the genre-mirror doctrine (the imported prophecy carried in the native prophetic metre - the corpus's reception-datum: how the North read foreign dooms through its own). In the atlas, the record anchors the learned-romance family: each a tradition's imported-myth register; the Norse one is distinctive in the metre.\n\nFor the database, this node documents the late-medieval compendia: the reception-file's learned layer.\n\nThe file's translation-method completes the register: the romances' Norse renderings documented (the saga-prose's domestication of the classical and British materials: the heroes renamed, the geography relocated, the Christian frame added), so the learned-reception file documents the import's adaptation: how the North's translators naturalized the foreign dooms and dynasties. And the corpus's afterlife completes it: the r\xEDmur-tradition's continuation (the later verse-cycles reworking the imported material) - the learned layer's reception documented through the post-medieval centuries.\n\nThe file's verse-craft completes the register: Merl\xEDn\xFAssp\xE1's metre documented (the eddic fornyr\xF0islag carrying the French prophecies - the translation's formal choices itemized), so the learned-reception file documents the import at the level of metre: the foreign doom fitted to the native form, stanza by stanza. And the Hauksbok-context completes it: the compilation's program (Haukr Erlendsson's law-book and the learned texts bound together - the imports shelved beside the native law) - the learned layer's library documented as one household's canon.\n\n The file\u2019s prophecy-genre junction completes it: the Voluspa-sibyl and Merlin read as the North\u2019s two prophet-voices - the imported seer naturalized beside the native one, the learned-reception file\u2019s genre-mirror closed.\n\n The file's Haukr-Erlendsson signature completes it: the compilation)s compiler documented (the law-man)s hand in the learned layer - the imports) patron named), the learned-reception file)s library traced to its owner."
    },
