        id: "2",
        text: "To this purpose, likewise, is that inscription which they have engraved upon the base of the statue of Athene at Sais, whom they identify with Isis: 'I am everything that has been, that is, and that shall be: and my veil no man hath raised.'",
        note: "Verbatim excerpt of Budge, Legends of the Gods (1912), Plutarch, De Iside sec. IX, quoted here as the Sais-temple parallel to the Neith tradition."
