    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Pei Hang, richly dressed and riding home from a failed examination, stopped at the Blue-Bridge station for water; behind the partition a girl's voice sang three lines that matched his own heart's verse \u2014 Yunying, the innkeeper's daughter, who was not of the innkeeper's stock.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Taiping Guangji, juan 50, Pei Hang entry (compiler's rendering); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "The old hostess named a bride-price no man could pay: a jade pestle and mortar of the immortals, and a hundred days of pounding the herb that opens the Way. Pei Hang sold his estates, hunted the jade through the markets of the capital, found it, and came back to the Blue Bridge to work.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Taiping Guangji, juan 50; not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "3",
        text: "A hundred days he pounded in the courtyard, hands in the drizzle, herbs to powder, powder to medicine; on the last night the doors of the inn opened on a hill of light, and the household came up the mountain as immortal guests. Years after, travelers saw two riders on a jade lion in the clouds and knew the pairing at the Blue Bridge had ended in heaven's register.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Taiping Guangji, juan 50, the ascent; not verbatim."
      }
    ],
