    license: "Public domain (Budge 1911)",
    summary: {
      en: "A census of the otherworld: an obscure passage in the Book of the Dead mentions 4,601,200 (or 4,301,200) spirit-souls (khu); the spirits who reap the wheat and barley in the Domain of Osiris are nine cubits tall against five-cubit corn, and in the Fifth Division the spirits who live on the helpless shadows of the dead have thighs seven cubits long \u2014 'Though naturally of a gay and light-hearted disposition, the Egyptian must have lived in a perpetual state of fear of spirits of all kinds.'",
      zh: "\u51A5\u754C\u4E4B\u6236\u7C4D\uFF1A\u4EA1\u9748\u66F8\u4E00 obscure \u6BB5\u843D\u8F09\u6709\u300E\u56DB\u767E\u516D\u5341\u842C\u96F6\u4E00\u5343\u4E8C\u767E\uFF08\u6216\u56DB\u767E\u4E09\u5341\u842C\u96F6\u4E00\u5343\u4E8C\u767E\uFF09\u4E4B\u9748\u300F\uFF1B\u65BC\u5967\u897F\u91CC\u65AF\u4E4B\u9818\u5208\u9EA5\u8005\u9AD8\u4E5D\u8098\u800C\u9EA5\u9AD8\u4E94\u8098\uFF1B\u7B2C\u4E94\u5340\u4EE5\u4EA1\u8005\u4E4B\u7121\u52A9\u4E4B\u5F71\u70BA\u98DF\u8005\uFF0C\u5176\u80A1\u9577\u4E03\u8098\u2014\u2014\u300E\u57C3\u53CA\u4EBA\u5929\u6027\u6A02\u5929\uFF0C\u7136\u5FC5\u6046\u5C45\u65BC\u5C0D\u8AF8\u9748\u4E4B\u6050\u61FC\u4E4B\u4E2D\u3002\u300F"
    },
    motifs: [
      "descent-underworld",
      "spirit-possession",
      "celestial-bureaucracy",
      "secret-book"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Ancient funerary cosmology via Budge 1911; no living community restrictions."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "An obscure passage in the Book of the Dead mentions 4,601,200, or 4,301,200, Spirit-souls (Khu), but whether these represented all the inhabitants of the spirit-world of Egypt cannot be said. In the Short Version of the Chapter '12 cubits' are mentioned, and this may be the height of the spirits. If so, spirits must have been of varying heights, for the spirits who reaped the wheat and barley in the Second Division of the Domain of Osiris were nine cubits in height, the wheat and barley being five cubits high. In the Fifth Division the spirits who lived on the helpless shadows of the dead had thighs (?) seven cubits long.",
        note: "Verbatim excerpt of Budge, Osiris and the Egyptian Resurrection vol. II (1911), ch. XX, citing Book of the Dead ch. 64 and ch. 149."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Now, we read in many funerary texts of the 'Gods of the Tuat,' so we must assume that after death entered the world, and souls began to go to the Tuat, they found there these gods, who had been created by the unknown God... As time went on these gods became more and more independent, and the unknown God appears to have allowed them to do as they pleased, and in the end they became the arbiters of the destinies of the souls of men. Though naturally of a gay and light-hearted disposition, the Egyptian must have lived in a perpetual state of fear of spirits of all kinds.",
        note: "Verbatim excerpt of Budge (1911), ch. XX."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "osiris"
    ]
