        id: "2",
        text: "There is in this sacred enclosure a house of Leto made of one single stone as regards both height and length, and of which all the walls are in these two directions equal, each being forty cubits; and for the covering in of the roof there lies another stone upon the top, the cornice measuring four cubits.",
        note: "Verbatim excerpt of Macaulay (1890), Book II.155."
