        id: "1",
        text: "Amasis also dedicated in Sais the chamber of the temple of Athene, which is over against the entrance; it is of the length of one-and-twenty cubits, and the breadth fourteen cubits, made of one single stone... the stone was brought from the town of Elephantine by the river, a distance of twenty days' journey: and the matter of the transport was the work of two thousand chosen men allotted to the class of boatmen, and this class of men had this business in charge for three years.",
        note: "Verbatim excerpt of Macaulay, Herodotus (1890), Book II.175."
