    period: "Mythical zoology recorded by Griffis, Corea: The Hermit Nation (1882)",
    source: {
      archive: "Project Gutenberg",
      work: "William Elliot Griffis, Corea: The Hermit Nation (1882), ch. 33, eBook #67141",
      url: "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/67141"
    },
    license: "Public domain (1882)",
    summary: {
      en: "The in-e, fish-man or merman, is a sort of siren supposed to inhabit the Sea of Japan and the Eastern Sea. It is six or seven feet long, and in head and body resembles a human being, its nose, mouth, ears and arms or flippers covered with white skin without scales; it has a long slender tail like a horse's. It suckles its young and sheds tears when its offspring are captured \u2014 and perhaps this is the creature around Quelpart whose tears produce pearls.",
      zh: "\u6771\u6D77\u6709\u4EBA\u9B5A\uFF0C\u9577\u516D\u4E03\u5C3A\uFF0C\u9996\u8EAB\u4F3C\u4EBA\uFF0C\u9F3B\u53E3\u8033\u81C2\u7686\u6709\u767D\u819A\u7121\u9C57\uFF0C\u5C3E\u7D30\u9577\u5982\u99AC\u5C3E\u3002\u80FD\u54FA\u4E73\u5176\u5B50\uFF0C\u5B50\u70BA\u4EBA\u6240\u7372\u5247\u6CE3\u3002\u6216\u8B02\u6FDF\u5DDE\u6D77\u4E2D\u4EA6\u6709\u5176\u985E\uFF0C\u5176\u6DDA\u5316\u70BA\u73E0\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "transformation",
      "world-serpent"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Folk-zoology record; no living-community restriction."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "The in-e, fish-man or merman, is a sort of siren that is supposed to inhabit the Sea of Japan and the Eastern Sea, but whether partly fabulous or entirely real, we are unable to say. It is six or seven feet long, and in its head and body resembles a human being, as its nose, mouth, ears, and arms, or flippers, are covered with white skin without scales. It has a long and slender tail, like that of a horse. It suckles its young, and sheds tears when its offspring are captured. It is probable that this creature is the same as a reported dog-fish or shark living in the seas around Quelpart, whose tears produce pearls.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Griffis, Corea: The Hermit Nation, ch. 33 (1882); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: []
