    license: "Sixteenth-century texts public domain; Tozzer translation only paraphrased",
    summary: {
      en: "On the highest mound of Izamal stood the temple of Kinich Kakm\xF3, 'the sun with a face'. The first inhabitants of the city were remembered as founder-gods \u2014 Kinich Kabul, Kinich Kakmo, Cit Ah Cutz ('father of the turkey lineage'), Cit Ah Coyi ('father of the coyote lineage') \u2014 whose names became the patronymics of living families. From the temple's top one saw the whole land and the sea.",
      zh: "\u4F0A\u624E\u99AC\u723E\u6700\u9AD8\u7684\u4E18\u4E0A\uFF0C\u7ACB\u6709\u57FA\u5C3C\u5947\xB7\u5361\u514B\u83AB\u2014\u2014\u300C\u6709\u9762\u4E4B\u65E5\u300D\u2014\u2014\u7684\u795E\u5EDF\u3002\u57CE\u4E2D\u521D\u6C11\u88AB\u8A18\u70BA\u5275\u65CF\u4E4B\u795E\uFF1A\u57FA\u5C3C\u5947\xB7\u5361\u5E03\u723E\u3001\u57FA\u5C3C\u5947\xB7\u5361\u514B\u83AB\u3001\u897F\u7279\xB7\u963F\xB7\u5EAB\u8328\uFF08\u706B\u96DE\u6C0F\u4E4B\u7236\uFF09\u3001\u897F\u7279\xB7\u963F\xB7\u79D1\u4F0A\uFF08\u90CA\u72FC\u6C0F\u4E4B\u7236\uFF09\uFF0C\u5176\u540D\u6210\u70BA\u5F8C\u4E16\u5BB6\u65CF\u7684\u59D3\u6C0F\u3002\u81EA\u5EDF\u9802\u53EF\u671B\u5168\u5883\u8207\u5927\u6D77\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "sacred-place",
      "culture-hero",
      "theophany",
      "idol-contest"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Sixteenth-century colonial record; paraphrase of published translations only."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "There was also another mound at Izamal which is today the highest one, and it is called Kinich Kakmo, the reason being that there was a temple on top of it and in it an idol which had this name, which in our language means 'the sun with a face'. From the top of the chapel one sees wonderfully well, as far as the sight can reach, and the sea is visible.",
        note: "Condensed paraphrase of Lizana, Devocionario (1633), and Landa (Tozzer 1941); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "The first inhabitants of the city were Kinich Kabul, Kinich Kakmo, Cit Ah Cutz and Cit Ah Coyi, from whom descended the Xols, the Mos and the Coyes. These first inhabitants should be considered founder gods: their names became the surnames of the lineages that still bear them, so that the god of the sun-faced temple is also the ancestor in the count of families.",
        note: "Condensed paraphrase of the Relacion of Izamal and Lizana (Tozzer 1941); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "itzamna"
    ]
