    license: "Public domain (Bancroft 1883)",
    summary: {
      en: "In the same city was an image of Kinich Kakmo, 'face or eye of the sun', whom Landa represents as the offspring of the sun, but who subsequently became identified with that luminary. He is represented in the act of sacrifice, pointing the finger toward a ray from the midday sun, as if to draw a spark wherewith to kindle the sacred fire; to this idol the people resorted in times of calamity and sickness.",
      zh: "\u540C\u57CE\u6709\u57FA\u5C3C\u5947\xB7\u5361\u514B\u83AB\u4E4B\u50CF\u2014\u2014\u300C\u65E5\u4E4B\u9762\u6216\u76EE\u300D\u2014\u2014\u862D\u9054\u8A18\u5176\u70BA\u592A\u967D\u4E4B\u5B50\uFF0C\u5F8C\u8207\u592A\u967D\u5408\u4E00\u3002\u50CF\u4F5C\u737B\u796D\u4E4B\u72C0\uFF0C\u6307\u65E5\u4E2D\u5149\u8292\uFF0C\u4F3C\u6B32\u5F15\u53D6\u706B\u661F\u4EE5\u71C3\u8056\u706B\uFF1B\u51E1\u906D\u707D\u75C5\uFF0C\u6C11\u7686\u8A63\u6B64\u6C42\u8AED\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "fire-theft",
      "theophany",
      "oracle-divination",
      "idol-contest"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Compendium of sixteenth-century colonial sources; paraphrase of public-domain text only."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "In the same city was an image of Kinich Kakmo, 'face or eye of the sun', whom Landa represents to be the offspring of the sun, but who subsequently became identified with that luminary and received divine honors in the very temple that he had erected to his father. He is represented in the act of sacrifice, pointing the finger toward a ray from the midday sun, as if to draw a spark wherewith to kindle the sacred fire. To this idol the people resorted in times of calamity and sickness, bringing offerings to induce oracular advice. Lizana translates the name as 'Sol con rostro' \u2014 the sun with a face whose rays are of fire.",
        note: "Condensed from Bancroft (1883), ch. XI; not verbatim throughout."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "itzamna"
    ]
