        text: "It was the custom of Yucatec wayfarers, when passing some prominent point on the road or spot where an image of Echuah stood, to add a stone or two to the heap already accumulated there, an act of devotion similar to that performed by the Romans in honor of Mercury. Echuah, or the Holy Ghost, was the patron god of merchants and travelers.",
