    license: "Public domain (Cogolludo 1688)",
    summary: {
      en: "They went to the pueblo of Coba, now depopulated, and there it was that the Spaniards were called by the Indians in their language Ah makal kopob, which means the eaters of anonas, a fruit of that land; the Indians, amazed, watched them eat the fruit without considering whether it was noxious or not.",
      zh: "\u4ED6\u5011\u884C\u81F3\u79D1\u5DF4\u6751\uFF08\u4ECA\u5DF2\u8352\u856A\uFF09\uFF1B\u6B63\u662F\u5728\u90A3\u88E1\uFF0C\u897F\u73ED\u7259\u4EBA\u88AB\u571F\u4EBA\u4EE5\u571F\u8A9E\u7A31\u70BA\u300C\u963F\xB7\u99AC\u5361\u723E\xB7\u79D1\u6CE2\u5E03\u300D\u2014\u2014\u98DF\u756A\u8354\u679D\u8005\uFF0C\u756A\u8354\u679D\u4E43\u7576\u5730\u679C\u7269\u3002\u571F\u4EBA\u9A5A\u7570\u5730\u770B\u4ED6\u5011\u5403\u9019\u679C\u5B50\uFF0C\u5168\u7136\u4E0D\u554F\u5176\u662F\u5426\u6709\u6BD2\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "trickster",
      "taboo-transgression"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Seventeenth-century colonial record; paraphrase of the Spanish original."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "They passed to the pueblo of Coba, now depopulated, and there it was that the Spaniards were called by the Indians in their language Ah makal kopob, which means the eaters of anonas, which is a fruit of that land: the Indians were amazed to see them eat them without considering whether they were noxious or not.",
        note: "Condensed paraphrase of Cogolludo (1688), lib. II; not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "gagavitz"
    ]
