        text: "In the prayers given before the idols, the other and lesser deities are invoked to come and carry the sacrifices offered and present them to 'the great lord.' Two flowers, the red Plumeria and the white Plumeria, are considered the father and mother respectively of Nohochakyum; one of each kind is placed on the mouth of the brasero containing the idol of Nohochakyum.",
