    lat: 49.9,
    lon: 30.6,
    period: "Event of 988; recorded in the Russian Primary Chronicle (Cross translation 1930); retold by Machal 1918",
    source: {
      archive: "Wikisource / Internet Archive",
      work: "Jan Machal, Slavic Mythology, Mythology of All Races III (1918), Part III ch. 1",
      url: "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Mythology_of_All_Races/Volume_3/Slavic/Part_3"
    },
    license: "Public domain (1918)",
    summary: {
      en: "When Vladimir was baptized in 988 he ordered the idols broken or burned; Perun alone was tied to a horse's tail, dragged down to the stream, beaten by twelve men to disgrace the demon who had deceived men, and pushed through the rapids \u2014 landing forever on the sands called Perunya Ren, Perun's Sands.",
      zh: "\u4E5D\u516B\u516B\u5E74\u5F17\u62C9\u57FA\u7C73\u723E\u53D7\u6D17\uFF0C\u547D\u6BC0\u8AF8\u795E\u50CF\uFF1B\u7368\u4F69\u502B\u50CF\u88AB\u7E6B\u65BC\u99AC\u5C3E\u3001\u62D6\u81F3\u6CB3\u908A\uFF0C\u5341\u4E8C\u4EBA\u7B1E\u4E4B\uFF0C\u4EE5\u8FB1\u60D1\u773E\u4E4B\u9B54\uFF0C\u4E26\u63A8\u5176\u904E\u7058\u2014\u2014\u795E\u50CF\u7D42\u64F1\u6DFA\u65BC\u5F8C\u4E16\u7A31\u300E\u4F69\u502B\u7058\u300F\u4E4B\u6C99\u6D32\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "taboo-transgression",
      "transformation",
      "sacred-kingship",
      "conversion",
      "idol-contest"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Chronicle source."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "When Prince Vladimir received baptism in 988 he went to Kiev and ordered all idols to be broken, cut to pieces, or thrown into the fire. The statue of Perun, however, was tied to a horse's tail and dragged down to a brook, where twelve men beat it with rods \u2014 not because the wood could feel pain, but that the demon which had deceived men might be disgraced.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Machal, Slavic Mythology, Mythology of All Races III (1918), Part III ch. 1, after the Primary Chronicle; not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "As the idol was carried to the Dnieper the pagans wept, for they had not yet been baptized. When it was thrown into the river Vladimir gave the command: 'If it stops, thrust it from the banks until it has passed the rapids; then let it alone.' The order was carried out, and no sooner had the idol passed through the rapids than it was cast upon the sands, which after that time were called Perunya Ren \u2014 Perun's Sands. Where the image once stood Vladimir built a church of St. Basil; yet Perun's worship did not finally disappear from the land until the end of the eleventh century.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Machal, Slavic Mythology, Mythology of All Races III (1918), Part III ch. 1; not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "perun"
    ]
