    license: "Public domain (1918)",
    summary: {
      en: "Dazhbog, 'the Giving God', Czar-Sun and Son of Svarog, stood beside Perun on the Kiev hill; early Russian texts translate Helios by his name, and the Tale of Igor's Campaign calls the princes of Russia his grandchildren \u2014 while in Serbian fairy-tale he lingers as Dabog, the tsar on earth set against God in heaven.",
      zh: "\u9054\u65E5\u535A\u683C\u2014\u2014\u300E\u65BD\u4E88\u4E4B\u795E\u300F\u3001\u592A\u967D\u6C99\u7687\u3001\u65AF\u74E6\u7F85\u683C\u4E4B\u5B50\u2014\u2014\u7ACB\u65BC\u57FA\u8F14\u4E18\u4E0A\u4F69\u502B\u4E4B\u5074\uFF1B\u53E4\u7F85\u65AF\u6587\u737B\u4EE5\u4E4B\u540D\u8B6F\u5E0C\u81D8\u4E4B\u8D6B\u5229\u4FC4\u65AF\uFF0C\u300A\u4F0A\u6208\u723E\u9060\u5F81\u8A18\u300B\u7A31\u7F85\u65AF\u738B\u516C\u70BA\u5176\u5B6B\uFF1B\u585E\u723E\u7DAD\u4E9E\u7AE5\u8A71\u4E2D\u7336\u5B58\u70BA\u9054\u535A\u683C\u2014\u2014\u5730\u4E0A\u4E4B\u6C99\u7687\uFF0C\u8207\u5929\u4E0A\u4E4B\u795E\u76F8\u5C0D\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "sacred-kingship",
      "sun-capture",
      "divine-marriage"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Chronicle source."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "The statue of Dazhbog, whose name probably means 'the Giving God', stood on the hill in the courtyard of the castle at Kiev beside the idols of Perun, Khors, and Stribog. Old chronicles term him 'Czar Sun' and 'Son of Svarog'; early Russian texts frequently translate the name of the Greek Helios as Dazhbog, which may be taken as proof that he was worshipped as a solar deity.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Machal, Slavic Mythology, Mythology of All Races III (1918), Part III ch. 2; not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "In the old Russian epic, the Tale of Igor's Campaign, Vladimir and the Russians call themselves the grandchildren of Dazhbog \u2014 the ancient Slavs often derived their origin from divine beings. Dazhbog was known among the Southern Slavs too, his memory preserved in the Serbian fairy-tale of Dabog: 'Dabog, the Czar, was on earth, and the Lord God was in heaven' \u2014 the old pagan sun-king refigured as an evil being, since early Christianity counted the old gods devilish.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Machal, Slavic Mythology, Mythology of All Races III (1918), Part III ch. 2; not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "svarog",
      "perun"
    ]
