        id: "1",
        text: "Stribog, whose idol stood on the hill in Kiev beside that of Perun, was most probably the god of cold and frost. In the Tale of Igor's Campaign the winds are called 'the grandsons of Stribog' \u2014 a conception of the winds as the result of cold and frost, children and children's children of the frozen god.",
