        text: "The citizens rejoiced and gathered the birds. Olga gave her soldiers a command, saying to each: 'Tie a match to each pigeon and sparrow, with a small piece of cloth wrapped in sulphur and bound with thread.' When darkness fell she released the birds, and each flew to its own nest \u2014 to the pigeon-coops, the pigeon-perches, and the eaves \u2014 and so the dove-cotes, the roofs, the porches, and the hayricks caught fire, and there was not a house that was not consumed, so that all fled in flight from the city. The people who escaped were taken prisoner, the city burned, the first citizens slain, others made to pay tribute.",
