        id: "1",
        text: "As for the sun's daughter, the golden cock crows on the edge of the Great Water \u2014 the Daugawa \u2014 to rouse her that she may spin the silver thread, that is, the rays of the rising sun. Her chief task is to wash her golden jug \u2014 the solar disk \u2014 at evening; her morning task is the spinning of the silver thread on the golden wheel. Between cockcrow and sundown the daughter of the sun keeps the sky's household running: the cock, the spinner, and the washer are the three servants of the light, and the dainas give each his hour.",
