        id: "1",
        text: "The way they marched to all was known; custom had made that track their own. 'Twas to those rovers mere child's play to plunder there, sometimes to slay, and often to enslave; and all the peaceful tribes who dwelt around \u2014 the heavy hand had felt \u2014 of Caribs, fierce and brave. Their large canoes were often seen as they sailed round from Marowijne and Surinam to Corentyne, then towards that river's head. Above the falls they cross Berbice, and march where all is perfect peace.",
        note: "Condensed paraphrase of Brett 1880, 'The Carib War Path'; not verbatim."
