    title: {
      en: "Kanaima: the Vow, the Jaguar, and the Blood at the Grave",
      zh: "\u5361\u5948\u746A\uFF1A\u6BD2\u8A93\u3001\u7F8E\u6D32\u8C79\u8207\u5893\u524D\u4E4B\u8840"
    },
    tradition: "amazonian",
    category: "myth",
    region: {
      en: "From Roraima to the Eastern sea (Akawai)",
      zh: "\u81EA\u7F85\u8CF4\u99AC\u81F3\u6771\u6D77\uFF08\u963F\u5361\u74E6\uFF09"
    },
    lat: 4.5,
    lon: -59,
    period: "Akawai oral tradition; recorded 1880 (Brett)",
    source: {
      archive: "Internet Archive",
      work: "W. H. Brett, Legends and Myths of the Aboriginal Indians of British Guiana (1880), Part IV 'Legends of the Acawoios', 'Kanaima'",
      url: "https://archive.org/details/cu31924020443218"
    },
    license: "Public domain (book 1880)",
    summary: {
      en: "From the base of high Roraima to the widespread Eastern sea, votaries of dread Kanaima track their victims secretly. Deadly vow must each fulfil, real or fancied foe to kill: he who that dread vow is taking, family and friends must leave \u2014 wife and children all forsaking, no discharge can he receive; still around his victim's way, hovering night and day to slay. Stealthily each step he traces, hiding till he strikes the blow; poison in the mouth he places of his victim, lying low; then, if found with swollen tongue, none will know who did him wrong. When the grave has closed upon him the destroyer hovers round: dread Kanaima's spell is on him, by it he must still be bound, till he pierce with pointed wood through the grave, and taste the blood \u2014 stern Kanaima thus appeasing, who withdraws his direful aid. One who passed on the Upper Demerara in 1865 was fresh from slaughter, hastening home again: a feathered crown adorned his head \u2014 bright red spots his skin o'erspread \u2014 spots, to show that, nightly ranging (so their sorcerers declare), he, into a jaguar changing, could his victims seize and tear, as the were-wolf of the East prowls on human flesh to feast. Should the victim escape him living, the spell upon him lies; mad, he wanders till he dies.",
      zh: "\u81EA\u7F85\u8CF4\u99AC\u4E4B\u9E93\u81F3\u6771\u6D77\u4E4B\u6FF1\uFF0C\u5361\u5948\u746A\u4E4B\u6BD2\u8A93\u8005\u5BC6\u8DE1\u7375\u5176\u4EC7\u3002\u7ACB\u8A93\u8005\u5FC5\u96E2\u5BB6\u5BA4\uFF0C\u8A93\u6210\u65B9\u514D\uFF1B\u65E5\u591C\u4F3A\u65BC\u4EC7\u4EBA\u4E4B\u9014\uFF0C\u5FCD\u800C\u5F85\u6A5F\u3002\u6BD2\u7F6E\u65BC\u5782\u6B7B\u8005\u53E3\u4E2D\uFF1B\u820C\u816B\u800C\u83AB\u77E5\u8AB0\u5F12\u3002\u5893\u65E2\u9589\uFF0C\u5831\u4EC7\u8005\u7336\u7E5E\u4E4B\uFF1A\u5361\u5948\u746A\u4E4B\u5492\u7E1B\u5176\u8EAB\uFF0C\u5FC5\u4EE5\u5C16\u6728\u523A\u5893\u3001\u98F2\u8840\u4E43\u89E3\u30021865\u5E74\u4E0A\u5FB7\u6885\u62C9\u62C9\u6CB3\u6709\u5E36\u8840\u800C\u6B78\u8005\uFF1A\u7FBD\u51A0\u5728\u9996\uFF0C\u808C\u6709\u7D05\u6591\u2014\u2014\u85A9\u6EFF\u8A00\u5176\u591C\u80FD\u5316\u7F8E\u6D32\u8C79\uFF0C\u566C\u5176\u4EC7\u4EBA\uFF0C\u5982\u6771\u65B9\u4E4B\u72FC\u4EBA\u4E5F\u3002\u4EC7\u82E5\u5F97\u812B\uFF0C\u5492\u4E0D\u96E2\u8EAB\uFF1B\u72C2\u8D70\u81F3\u6B7B\u3002"
    },
