        text: "Amongst the starres they all did commonly worship that which they called Colca, and we here the little goates [the Pleiades]... as the shepheard did sacrifice to a star which they called vrcuchillay, which they holde to be a sheepe of divers colours, having the care to preserve their cattell. It is understood to be that which the Astronomers call Lyra. These shepheards worshippe two other starres, which walke neere vnto them, they call them Catuchillay and vrcuchillay; and they faine them to be an ewe and a lambe.",
        note: "Condensed paraphrase of Acosta, Natural and Moral History, book 5 ch. 4 (Hakluyt Society 1880); not verbatim."
