    persons: [],
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Sailing of Lono to Oahu, and the arrival of Ohaikawiliula: Lono's contest with Kakuhihewa, then the wager made by Kakuhihewa against Lono, and the second to fifth contests, with the arrival of Kaikilani - Lonoikamakahiki proving his worth at the konane board, the Hawaiian checkers, game after game against the king of Oahu.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Fornander Collection of Hawaiian Folk-lore, vol. 4, Story of Lonoikamakahiki (1916-1917); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "The dispute between Kakuhihewa and Lono about the hiding-place of the bones of the chiefs slain by Keawenuiaumi ends with Lono revealing the secret grave - how Lono revealed the bones of chiefs slain by Keawenuiaumi being the eighth chapter of his story. Winning each trial Lono returns to Hawaii, where Kaikilani, the first chiefess ruler, receives him, and together they deal with the rebellious chiefs at Napoopoo - the exploits of the great soldier of victories, who conquered Oahu at the games if not on the field.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Fornander Collection of Hawaiian Folk-lore, vol. 4, Story of Lonoikamakahiki (1916-1917); not verbatim."
      }
    ]
