        id: "1",
        text: "Makolea arriving at Kauai becomes wife of Kaikipaananea, one of the three strong men of Oahu, in boxing beaten by Kepakailiula and in wrestling matches; Kukaea, who lived on filth, threw Kaikipaananea into the oven, and Kepakailiula, befriended by a high chief under Kaikipaananea, came to avenge him - Kepakailiula befriended by the high chief who sheltered him in Kauai.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Fornander Collection of Hawaiian Folk-lore, vol. 4, Legend of Kepakailiula (1916-1917); not verbatim."
