        id: "1",
        text: "The mother-in-law of Zilizoaibu gave her son-in-law K\xE4liwa\xFC-fish to eat: she took an old calabash, set it under herself and pressed her belly together, whereupon the fish came out of her uterus and fell into the calabash \u2014 that is why the Taulipang do not eat this fish to this day. The fish she gave to her son-in-law and to her daughter Way\xFClal\xEB to eat; the latter knew nothing of it. But the son-in-law knew it, for he was a shaman.",
