        id: "1",
        text: "When none fared ill at court, Barbad heard tell of the minstrel Mardwi, and Barbad approached Mardwi forthwith; the Shah is coming to the pleasance, said Barbad, and dressed all in green and took his harp. And thought the Shah: none but Barbad can play so. Then while Barbad sang on the monarch quaffed. He filled the singer's mouth. Barbad became the first of harpers. The epoch of Barbad hath past and gone: that market never failed while he could strike the strings.",
