        text: "He formerly sang, while he uttered the Stars' names. He said '\\whai' to (some) Stars which are very small; they are those of which he made '\\whai'; their small, fine ones are those which are '\\whai'. [The stars \\whai-gwai and \\whai-|pua were identified as Altair and neighbouring stars of Aquila.]",
        note: "Quote from Specimens of Bushman Folklore (Bleek & Lloyd 1911), p. 79 with editor's bracketed note (public domain)."
