        id: "4",
        text: "Condensed paraphrase of Bleek's 1875 summary (\xA725): the mother of the Dawn's-Heart-child was the Lynx, who was then a beautiful woman; she was bewitched with poisoned Bushman rice and transformed into a lioness; her brothers pulled off the lion skin so that she became a fair woman again; but, in consequence of having been bewitched by Bushman rice, she could no longer eat that, and was changed into a lynx who ate meat.",
        note: "Condensed paraphrase of A Brief Account of Bushman Folk-lore (Bleek 1875), \xA725; not verbatim."
