    license: "Public domain (Schiefner/Ralston translation 1882)",
    summary: {
      en: "Seeing the moon's reflection in a well, a monkey-leader cries that the moon has fallen in and the world is without a moon - must they not draw it out? They form a chain, the first hanging from a branch and each from the tail above; the branch bends, the water is troubled, the reflection vanishes, the branch breaks, and all fall into the well - 'when the foolish have a foolish leader they all go to ruin.'",
      zh: "\u7334\u738B\u898B\u4E95\u4E2D\u6708\u5F71\uFF0C\u9A5A\u547C\u6708\u843D\u4E95\u4E2D\u3001\u5929\u4E0B\u7121\u6708\uFF0C\u6025\u9808\u6488\u8D77\u3002\u773E\u7334\u7D50\u93C8\uFF0C\u9996\u7334\u61F8\u6A39\u679D\uFF0C\u4F9D\u6B21\u6293\u5C3E\uFF1B\u6A39\u679D\u5F4E\u66F2\uFF0C\u6C34\u52D5\u5F71\u6563\uFF0C\u679D\u65B7\u7334\u589C\uFF0C\u76E1\u843D\u4E95\u4E2D\u2014\u2014\u300C\u611A\u8005\u9047\u611A\u4E3B\uFF0C\u540C\u6B78\u65BC\u76E1\u3002\u300D"
    },
    motifs: [
      "parable-teaching",
      "trickster",
      "mirror"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Kah-gyur fable literature; this episode parallels the widely known monkey-and-moon story across Buddhist Asia."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "The leader said: the moon has fallen into the well; the world is now without a moon; ought not we to draw it out? They formed a chain, the first monkey hanging on to the branch of a tree and each to the tail above; the branch bent a good deal, the water was troubled, the reflection of the moon disappeared, the branch broke, and all the monkeys fell into the well and were disagreeably damaged. A deity sang: when the foolish have a foolish leader, they all go to ruin.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Schiefner/Ralston, The Monkeys and the Moon (1882); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: []
