        text: "Ha ha ha, Ha ha, I am the one whom the Lynx derides, I am the one who did not run fast; For, the Lynx is the one who runs fast. It did foolish things; For, the Lynx is one who understands, The Cat does not understand. The Cat (nevertheless) is cunning. It had to be cunning. For, the Lynx is one who is cunning. Reference is here made to the Cat's way of doubling when pursued.",
        note: "Quote from Specimens of Bushman Folklore (Bleek & Lloyd 1911), p. 221 (public domain). / Quote from Specimens of Bushman Folklore (Bleek & Lloyd 1911), p. 222 (public domain). / Quote from Specimens of Bushman Folklore (Bleek & Lloyd 1911), p. 222 with note (public domain)."
