        id: "1",
        text: "Asag rises in the mountains: his heat makes the land's edge boil, fevers run from river to river, and the stones rally to him. Ninurta's mace Sharur flies to him and speaks: the master must fight, for the demon defies the gods' order. Ninurta meets Asag by the rivers, forty and more, each battle a separate river-name; Asag's mother, weary of her son's deformity, works against him too. The warrior god prevails and the demon falls.",
