        text: "To every power of the mountain \u2014 the cave's lord, the river's god, the Anuna of the wild places \u2014 he presents his due, and none is slighted; the poem closes with the hero standing ready, his piety proven, for the meeting the mountains will now grant him.",
        note: "Paraphrase of ETCSL c.1.8.2.1, the piety test passed; not verbatim."
