        id: "1",
        text: "Ludingira, traveling far, writes to his mother at Ur-Namma's house: mother, do not be anxious for me \u2014 the courier is sound, the roads are safe, and your son thinks of you. The poem's tenderness is its theme: the mother's worry set against the son's reassurance, love measured across the distances of empire \u2014 the earliest letter-poem of family love in world literature.",
        note: "Paraphrase of ETCSL c.5.5.1, the message; not verbatim. / Paraphrase of ETCSL c.5.5.1, the tenderness; not verbatim."
