        id: "2",
        text: "Condensed paraphrase, same locus; not verbatim. A bobbejaan demanded the necklace thong, made of his brother's skin, and warned he would return with a commando of his brothers to break the huts. The Mantis changed his son into a great bird and the child into the Echo; the bird's wings raised a great wind, and a terrible whirlwind hurled stones and sticks until the bobbejaans scattered and fled.",
