    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "By far the most popular teacher in Tibet during this reign, after Sambhava's death, was Kamalagila. He at first met with a great deal of opposition from the Chinese Hwa-shang, the most influential of which was called Mahayana or Mahadeva; Kamalagila defeated him in a grand controversy held in the king's presence, and from that time the Madhyamika doctrines were generally followed. Besides translating a great many Buddhist works into Tibetan, he wrote a large number of treatises which are still extant in the Tengyur - in the sutra section alone seventeen works written by him.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Rockhill, The Life of the Buddha (1884); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "songtsen-gampo"
    ]
