    motifs: [
      "theophany",
      "ritual-origin",
      "sacred-kingship",
      "incarnation-avatar",
      "origin-livestock"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Historical-legendary material; paraphrase of public-domain translation."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Vijayasambhava was an incarnation of Maitreya and Manjushri; having assumed the form of a Bhikshu, the Arya Vairochana came and dwelt in the Tsu-la grove in the country of Tsar-ma, became the spiritual guide of the inhabitants of Li-yul, taught the ignorant cattle-herders in the Li language, and invented the characters of Li - after this the Dharma appeared.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Rockhill, The Life of the Buddha (1884); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "King Vijayasambhava built the great vihara of Tsar-ma, but he greatly longed for some relics of the body of the Tathagata; he was told to build a chaitya, and when the vihara was finished, Vairochana told the king to sound the ganta and to invite the Aryas. He replied, may I never sound the ganta unless the Tathagata comes here and gives me a ganta! Immediately Vairochana assumed the appearance of the Tathagata, and after having taught like the Tathagata sixty great dharmas at Tsar-ma, he gave King Vijayasambhava a ganta, and the king sounded it without ceasing for seven days.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Rockhill, The Life of the Buddha (1884); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: []
