        id: "3",
        text: "Whosoever shall smite either a shepherd's dog, or a house dog, or a Vohunazga dog, or a trained dog, his soul when passing to the other world shall fly amid louder howling and fiercer pursuing than the sheep does when the wolf rushes upon it in the lofty forest. No soul will come and meet his departing soul and help it through the howls and pursuit in the other world; nor will the dogs that keep the Chinvat bridge help his departing soul.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Vendidad Fargard XIII, 8-9 (Darmesteter, SBE 4, 1880); not verbatim."
