    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Ken Arok, a restless man of the village, serves the ruler of Tumapel while plotting his rise; the cursed kris Kyai Tanting Kembang, forged in blood and grudge, is set to kill for him until it finds its final victim in Tunggul Ametung, the ruler himself.",
        note: "Paraphrase of the Pararaton's Ken Angrok narrative; not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Ken Arok takes the widow Ken Dedes as his wife \u2014 already with child by the murdered ruler, and already marked by the prophecy that whoever possesses her bears kings. From that marriage the Singhasari dynasty is founded, and the chronicle's history of Java begins in a murder it never hides.",
        note: "Paraphrase of the Pararaton narrative; not verbatim."
      }
    ],
