    license: "Public domain (1817)",
    summary: {
      en: "Kuwu Mangkubumi sends a pellet-shooter to fell what he takes for a large black monkey on the pandi tree \u2014 and the 'monkey' speaks: 'Don't shoot at me; go home and tell your master to come here himself.' Prabu Lutung Kasarung comes down, is offered to two elder daughters who refuse him, and is accepted gladly by the youngest, Niai Purba Sari \u2014 at whose wedding he lays aside the black monkey's skin and resumes his former beautiful appearance, establishing the line of Pakuan Pajajaran.",
      zh: "\u5EAB\u70CF\xB7\u8292\u5EAB\u5E03\u7C73\u9063\u7375\u624B\u5C04\u64CA\u6F58\u8FEA\u6A39\u4E0A\u7684\u300E\u5927\u9ED1\u7334\u300F\u2014\u2014\u300E\u7334\u300F\u7ADF\u958B\u53E3\uFF1A\u300E\u83AB\u5C04\u6211\uFF1B\u56DE\u5BB6\u544A\u4F60\u4E3B\u4EBA\u89AA\u81EA\u524D\u4F86\u3002\u300F\u666E\u62C9\u5E03\xB7\u9B6F\u901A\xB7\u5361\u85A9\u9B6F\u6069\u4E0B\u6A39\u76F8\u898B\uFF1B\u5169\u4F4D\u9577\u5973\u7686\u62D2\u5AC1\u4E4B\uFF0C\u552F\u5E7C\u5973\u59AE\u827E\xB7\u666E\u723E\u5DF4\xB7\u6C99\u8389\u6B23\u7136\u63A5\u7D0D\u2014\u2014\u5A5A\u79AE\u4E4B\u4E0A\uFF0C\u4ED6\u892A\u53BB\u9ED1\u7334\u4E4B\u76AE\uFF0C\u6062\u5FA9\u672C\u4F86\u4FCA\u7F8E\u5BB9\u8C8C\uFF0C\u5E15\u5EAB\u5B89\xB7\u5DF4\u67E5\u67E5\u862D\u738B\u671D\u7531\u6B64\u800C\u7ACB\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "transformation",
      "miraculous-birth",
      "sacred-kingship"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Sundanese founding legend (Carita Parahyangan tradition as recorded by Raffles); animal-husband motif with divine identity."
    },
    language: "Sundanese",
    canonical_translation: "Raffles, History of Java (1817), English; paraphrase",
    narrative: {
      en: "The Sunda traditions that Raffles recorded in 1817 preserve West Java's founding myth in a form the lowland Javanese chronicles never tell: the god who comes as a monkey.\n\nBEGINNING: THE SPEAKING MONKEY. Kuwu Mangkubumi establishes his youngest daughter, Purba Sari, in the interior near the gadug tree, and sets a pellet-shooter to work the district. One day the shooter sees on the great pandi tree what looks like a large black monkey, and takes aim; the creature speaks: 'Don't shoot at me; you had better go home and tell your master to come here to me himself.' The shooter returns aghast, and his master comes to the tree, where Prabu Lutung Kasarung descends and talks with him \u2014 a being of such extraordinary accomplishment that the Kuwu takes him home delighted.\n\nMIDDLE: THE CHOICE OF DAUGHTERS. Wishing to attach so wondrous a creature to his house, the Kuwu offers him first to the eldest daughter, who refuses; then to a younger, who refuses likewise. Only the youngest of all, Niai Purba Sari, accepts him with great pleasure \u2014 the marriage goes to the daughter humble enough to take the suitor as he appears.\n\nEND: THE SKIN LAID ASIDE. When Niai Purba Sari becomes his wife, he lays aside the black monkey's skin and resumes his former, beautiful appearance; he receives the name of Niang Galarang, establishes himself at Pakuan Pajajaran \u2014 where the inscribed stone stands \u2014 and governs there. His wife becomes pregnant; he leaves the government to his ministers and withdraws to Bukit Padang as a Pattala; and their son, Silawangi, will grow into the great king of the Sundanese chronicles.\n\nFUNCTIONS. The legend (1) grounds Pakuan Pajajaran, the Sundanese royal capital, in a divine-visitor marriage; (2) makes the acceptance of the humble appearance the test of rightful bride (the youngest-daughter motif); (3) ties kingship to the withdrawal of the god-founder into ascetic retreat; and (4) supplies the Sundanese counterpart to Java's Janggala-Kediri genealogies. The episode's social geometry repays attention: the Kuwu's household tests the suitor's appearance twice and both elder daughters decline, so that the divine visitor is accepted only by the youngest \u2014 the standard folktale marker of the daughter undervalued by her family, whose acceptance is rewarded with the god's true form and, through her son Silawangi, with the kingship of Pajajaran itself. The narrative also fixes two toponyms of the Sundanese landscape, the kampung Wangun and the kampung Tagur founded by the couple, and ends with the founder's characteristic withdrawal: as soon as the succession is secure, Niang Galarang leaves the seat of government to his ministers and removes to Bukit Padang as a Pattala, the ascetic retreat that later Sundanese tradition reads as the model of royal completion. In the full pantun tellings the monkey shape is the punishment of a heavenly exile, and the marriage that restores his form is the last condition of his return \u2014 the West Javanese version of the exiled-god theme that the Arjunawiwaha states in courtly verse.",
      zh: "\u62C9\u5F17\u723E\u65AF1817\u5E74\u6240\u9304\u5DFD\u4ED6\u7DE8\u5E74\u50B3\u8AAA\u4FDD\u5B58\u4E86\u897F\u722A\u54C7\u958B\u57FA\u795E\u8A71\uFF1A\u795E\u4EE5\u7334\u8EAB\u800C\u4F86\u3002\u5EAB\u70CF\xB7\u8292\u5EAB\u5E03\u7C73\u7F6E\u5E7C\u5973\u666E\u723E\u5DF4\xB7\u6C99\u8389\u65BC\u5167\u5730\u52A0\u90FD\u53E4\u6A39\u65C1\uFF1B\u7375\u624B\u898B\u6F58\u8FEA\u6A39\u4E0A\u300E\u9ED1\u7334\u300F\u800C\u7784\u6E96\uFF0C\u7334\u7ADF\u4EBA\u8A00\u3002\u9B6F\u901A\xB7\u5361\u85A9\u9B6F\u6069\u4E0B\u6A39\uFF0C\u624D\u83EF\u9A5A\u4EBA\uFF0C\u5EAB\u70CF\u651C\u6B78\u3002\u5EAB\u70CF\u6B32\u4EE5\u5973\u59BB\u4E4B\uFF1A\u9577\u5973\u62D2\u3001\u6B21\u5973\u62D2\uFF0C\u552F\u5E7C\u5973\u59AE\u827E\xB7\u666E\u723E\u5DF4\xB7\u6C99\u8389\u6B23\u7136\u63A5\u53D7\u3002\u5A5A\u5F8C\u795E\u892A\u7334\u76AE\u5FA9\u5176\u771F\u5BB9\uFF0C\u5F97\u540D\u5C3C\u63DA\xB7\u52A0\u62C9\u6717\uFF0C\u5EFA\u90FD\u5E15\u5EAB\u5B89\xB7\u5DF4\u67E5\u67E5\u862D\uFF08\u5373\u4ECA\u7891\u77F3\u4E4B\u5730\uFF09\uFF1B\u59BB\u6709\u5B55\u5F8C\uFF0C\u4ED6\u5C07\u570B\u653F\u59D4\u65BC\u5927\u81E3\uFF0C\u9000\u96B1\u5E03\u57FA\u7279\xB7\u5DF4\u7576\u70BA\u96B1\u8005\uFF1B\u5176\u5B50\u897F\u62C9\u842C\u5409\u5C07\u6210\u5DFD\u4ED6\u7DE8\u5E74\u53F2\u4E4B\u5049\u738B\u3002\u529F\u80FD\uFF1A\u4EE5\u795E\u5A5A\u7ACB\u5E15\u5EAB\u5B89\u738B\u90FD\u3001\u4EE5\u300E\u63A5\u7D0D\u5E73\u51E1\u5916\u8868\u300F\u70BA\u64C7\u5A7F\u8003\u9A57\uFF08\u5E7C\u5973\u6BCD\u984C\uFF09\u3001\u4EE5\u795E\u4E3B\u9000\u96B1\u7E6B\u738B\u6B0A\u65BC\u82E6\u4FEE\u3001\u4E26\u6210\u722A\u54C7\u7AE0\u683C\u62C9-\u8AEB\u7FA9\u91CC\u8B5C\u7CFB\u4E4B\u5DFD\u4ED6\u5C0D\u61C9\u3002"
    },
