        text: "Weaving at her loom, Dayang Sumbi drops the shuttle and vows that whoever returns it \u2014 man, animal, or god in any shape \u2014 shall be her husband; a dog brings it up the stair, and the vow is kept to the letter. The dog-god Tumang becomes her husband, the union scandalizes her father's house, and she is exiled \u2014 bearing in time the son Sangkuriang, whose own promise, years later, will shake the mountains.",
