    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "A mighty Javanese army invades the Minangkabau highlands; too few for open battle, the highlanders ask for terms, and the invader offers to settle the war by a single combat of buffaloes. The Minangkabau produce a starving calf with small knives honed and bound to its horns; set loose on the field, the calf runs straight at the great fighting bull nosing for milk, and its bound blades rip the beast open in the first charge. The invader keeps the wager and withdraws his army; the land is named Minangkabau \u2014 'the buffalo that won' \u2014 and the people roof their houses with horn-shaped gables in memory of the calf that beat a bull.",
        note: "Paraphrase of the Minangkabau name-legend; not verbatim."
      }
    ],
