        id: "1",
        text: "The tongkonan houses of the Toraja are founded by named ancestors and oriented to the cosmos; the house is the family's seat of memory, not merely its shelter. At every great feast and funeral, buffalo are sacrificed and their horns added to the facade; the growing wall of horns is a public genealogy of the house \u2014 rank, debt and descent read off the architecture itself.",
