        id: "1",
        text: "Both princes moved with their respective armies towards the centre of the island; a general engagement took place, which proving indecisive, a personal combat between the two chiefs was about to occur, when it was mutually agreed that thenceforth the countries to the west should be subject to Pajajaran, and those to the east to Majapahit. A line was drawn due south from a stone column placed near the spot in commemoration of the agreement; the column is still to be seen at Tigil, a few miles west of Semarang.",
