    lat: -6.7,
    lon: 107.4,
    period: "Performance recorded by Worsfold, A Visit to Java (1893)",
    source: {
      archive: "Internet Archive",
      work: "W. Basil Worsfold, A Visit to Java (1893), the wayang kulit performance observed",
      url: "https://archive.org/stream/avisittojavawit00worsgoog/avisittojavawit00worsgoog_djvu.txt"
    },
    license: "Public domain (1893)",
    summary: {
      en: "The wayang night observed in the round: the dalang sits cross-legged before the lamp, sticking the puppets into a banana-stem log taken from a box at his side; he chants 'a long legendary tale taken from the ancient Javan literature, dealing with the times before the European occupation of the island'; at intervals he breaks into dialogue, working the puppets' arms and legs with wires, while the gamelan orchestra behind him punctuates the play \u2014 and the audience sits 'listening for hours, far into the night, without getting tired.'",
      zh: "\u54C7\u63DA\u4E4B\u591C\u5168\u666F\uFF1A\u9054\u6717\u76E4\u5750\u71C8\u524D\uFF0C\u8EAB\u5074\u6728\u7BB1\u53D6\u5076\u3001\u63D2\u65BC\u9999\u8549\u8396\u5EA7\uFF1B\u4ED6\u541F\u5531\u300E\u53D6\u81EA\u53E4\u722A\u54C7\u6587\u5B78\u4E4B\u9577\u7BC7\u50B3\u8AAA\uFF0C\u6240\u8FF0\u4E43\u6B50\u4EBA\u64DA\u5CF6\u4E4B\u524D\u6642\u4EE3\u4E4B\u4E8B\u300F\uFF1B\u4E0D\u6642\u8F49\u5165\u5C0D\u767D\uFF0C\u4EE5\u9435\u7D72\u64CD\u7E31\u6232\u5076\u624B\u8DB3\uFF1B\u8EAB\u5F8C\u52A0\u7F8E\u862D\u6A02\u968A\u9EDE\u64CA\u4F34\u594F\u2014\u2014\u89C0\u773E\u300E\u4E45\u5750\u50BE\u807D\uFF0C\u76F4\u5230\u6DF1\u591C\u800C\u4E0D\u5026\u300F\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "ritual-origin",
      "parable-teaching",
      "theophany"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "The wayang performance as sacred recitation; read with the Batara Kala ruwatan record for the rite's protective office."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "The dalang sat before the lamp with the puppets stuck in a banana-stem log taken from a box placed by his side; he chanted a long legendary tale taken from the ancient Javan literature, dealing with the times before the European occupation of the island; at intervals he broke into a dialogue, when he worked the puppets' arms and legs with wires, so that they seemed to be acting their several parts.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Worsfold, A Visit to Java (1893); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Behind the dalang was a gamelan, a series of gongs on a wooden frame struck with wooden hammers by other members of the company; and it was interesting to observe the deep attention with which the audience followed the movements of the puppets and listened to the recitations \u2014 they would sit there listening for hours, far into the night, without getting tired.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Worsfold (1893); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
