      en: "Grieving at his son's grave, an old man is surprised by three visitors: one tall and long-nosed, one smaller and flat-nosed, the last very small and white as snow \u2014 the flat-nosed one asking for a piece of sole-leather, the white one for a piece of walrus-tooth. Seeing the departing guests bound off in the shape of a reindeer, a fox, and a hare \u2014 it is said the hare had need of something for a new tooth.",
