        id: "1",
        text: "Owl stole children. Coyote said: 'I'll be a child.' Coyote cried in the evening. He was told: 'You make a bad noise; Owl may almost take you away.' Coyote was taken; he was thrown out of the doorway. Owl took him along; he carried him along. He said: 'I am Coyote.' Owl was told: 'Let us dance!' Coyote and Owl danced; Coyote killed Owl, who had stolen the children. They started back. He said: 'I killed Owl.' Enough.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Kutenai Tales, p. 51 (Boas, 1918); not verbatim."
