        id: "2",
        text: "For Sarai's sake the LORD plagued Pharaoh and his house with great plagues. Pharaoh summoned Abram: 'Why didst thou not tell me that she was thy wife?' and sent him away with his wife and all he had. The epos of Israel's later affliction in Egypt begins, ironically, with its first forefather protected there by plague. Paraphrase of Genesis 12:16-20 (JPS 1917); not verbatim.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Genesis 12:16-20 (JPS 1917); not verbatim."
