        id: "2",
        text: "Abraham hurried Sarah to knead cakes, chose a calf, and set curds and milk before the men under the tree. 'Where is Sarah thy wife?' they asked, and repeated the promise. Sarah laughed within the tent, thinking of her worn body and her husband's age, and denied laughing \u2014 but the Visitor said: 'Nay; but thou didst laugh.' Paraphrase of Genesis 18:6-15 (JPS 1917); not verbatim.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Genesis 18:6-15 (JPS 1917); not verbatim."
