        id: "3",
        text: "And when they saw him afar off, even before he came near unto them, they conspired against him to slay him. And Reuben heard it, and he delivered him out of their hands; and said, Let us not kill him. And they stript Joseph out of his coat, his coat of many colours that was on him: and they took him, and cast him into a pit: and the pit was empty, there was no water in it. And Judah said unto his brethren, Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites. And they drew and lifted up Joseph out of the pit, and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt."
