    license: "Public domain (KJV, 1611)",
    summary: {
      en: "Breathing threatenings and slaughter, the persecutor travels to Damascus with warrants for 'this way'; suddenly a light from heaven shines around him and he falls to earth: 'Saul, Saul, why persecutest thou me?... I am Jesus whom thou persecutest: it is hard for thee to kick against the pricks.' Led blind into the city, he is met three days later by the disciple Ananias \u2014 'a chosen vessel unto me, to bear my name before the Gentiles' \u2014 receives his sight like scales falling, is baptized, and straightway preaches Christ in the synagogues.",
      zh: "\u53E3\u5410\u5A01\u5687\u5147\u6BBA\u8A71\u7684\u903C\u8FEB\u8005\uFF0C\u6301\u5927\u796D\u53F8\u516C\u6587\u5F80\u5927\u99AC\u58EB\u9769\u6349\u62FF\u300C\u4FE1\u5949\u9019\u9053\u7684\u4EBA\u300D\uFF1B\u5FFD\u7136\u5929\u4E0A\u6709\u5927\u5149\u56DB\u9762\u7167\u8457\u4ED6\uFF0C\u4ED6\u5C31\u4EC6\u5012\u5728\u5730\uFF1A\u300C\u6383\u7F85\uFF0C\u6383\u7F85\uFF0C\u4F60\u70BA\u751A\u9EBC\u903C\u8FEB\u6211\uFF1F\u2026\u2026\u6211\u5C31\u662F\u4F60\u6240\u903C\u8FEB\u7684\u8036\u7A4C\u3002\u4F60\u7528\u8173\u8E22\u523A\u662F\u96E3\u7684\u3002\u300D\u88AB\u62C9\u9032\u57CE\uFF0C\u4E09\u65E5\u770B\u4E0D\u898B\u3001\u4E0D\u5403\u4E0D\u559D\uFF1B\u9580\u5F92\u4E9E\u62FF\u5C3C\u4E9E\u5949\u547D\u53BB\u6309\u624B\u2014\u2014\u300C\u4ED6\u662F\u6211\u6240\u63C0\u9078\u7684\u5668\u76BF\uFF0C\u8981\u5728\u5916\u90A6\u4EBA\u548C\u541B\u738B\u4E26\u4EE5\u8272\u5217\u4EBA\u9762\u524D\u5BA3\u63DA\u6211\u7684\u540D\u300D\u2014\u2014\u9C57\u72C0\u7684\u6771\u897F\u6389\u4E0B\uFF0C\u4ED6\u5C31\u770B\u898B\uFF0C\u8D77\u4F86\u53D7\u6D17\uFF0C\u96A8\u5373\u5728\u5404\u6703\u5802\u5BA3\u8B1B\u8036\u7A4C\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "theophany",
      "theophany",
      "teacher-disciple",
      "conversion",
      "threefold"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Living tradition. The conversion is the hinge of Christian universalism; tagged theophany for the heavenly light and voice."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "And Saul, yet breathing out threatenings and slaughter against the disciples of the Lord, went unto the high priest, and desired of him letters to Damascus to the synagogues, that if he found any of this way, whether they were men or women, he might bring them bound unto Jerusalem. And as he journeyed, he came near Damascus: and suddenly there shined round about him a light from heaven: and he fell to the earth, and heard a voice saying unto him, Saul, Saul, why persecutest thou me? And he said, Who art thou, Lord? And the Lord said, I am Jesus whom thou persecutest: it is hard for thee to kick against the pricks."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "And Saul arose from the earth; and when his eyes were opened, he saw no man: but they led him by the hand, and brought him into Damascus. And he was three days without sight, and neither did eat nor drink. And there was a certain disciple at Damascus, named Ananias; and to him said the Lord in a vision, Ananias. And the Lord said unto him, Arise, and go into the street which is called Straight, and enquire in the house of Judas for one called Saul, of Tarsus: for, behold, he prayeth."
      },
      {
        id: "3",
        text: "But the Lord said unto him, Go thy way: for he is a chosen vessel unto me, to bear my name before the Gentiles, and kings, and the children of Israel: for I will shew him how great things he must suffer for my name's sake. And Ananias went his way, and entered into the house; and putting his hands on him said, Brother Saul, the Lord, even Jesus, that appeared unto thee in the way as thou camest, hath sent me, that thou mightest receive thy sight, and be filled with the Holy Ghost. And immediately there fell from his eyes as it had been scales: and he received sight forthwith, and arose, and was baptized."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "paul"
    ]
