    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Recite to them truly the story of the two sons of Adam. Each of them made an offering, and it was accepted from one of them and not accepted from the other. The rejected brother said, 'I will surely slay thee.' The other answered, 'God accepts only from the God-fearing; even if thou stretch out thy hand against me to slay me, I will not stretch out mine against thee, for I fear God, the Lord of all creatures. I would rather thou shouldst bear my sin and thine own, and become an inmate of the Fire \u2014 such is the reward of the unjust.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 5:27-29 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "His soul persuaded him to slay his brother, and he slew him, and became one of the lost. Then God sent a raven which scratched in the ground to show him how he might hide his brother's naked corpse. 'Woe is me!' he cried, 'am I unable to be like this raven, and to hide the body of my brother?' And he became one of the repentant. On account of this We commanded the children of Israel that whoever slays a soul, unless for a soul slain or for corruption done in the earth, it shall be as if he slew all mankind; and whoever saves one alive, it shall be as if he saved all mankind.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 5:30-32 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "adam"
    ]
