    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Sacred text of a living tradition, presented via public-domain translation; the 'Ad destruction is treated within Islam as a historical warning, not myth."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "And to 'Ad We sent their brother Hud. He said, 'O my people, worship God: ye have no other god than Him. Will ye not fear Him?' The unbelieving chiefs of his people answered, 'We see thee in folly, and we think thou art one of the liars. Shall we quit our gods at thy word? We see not that thou hast spoken truth; thou art one of the mockers.' He said, 'O my people, there is no folly in me; I am a messenger from the Lord of all creatures. The messages of my Lord I bring you, and I am your faithful counsellor.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 7:65-68 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "'Do ye build a landmark on every high place to amuse yourselves? And get you strong places, haply to abide for ever? And when you seize, do you seize as tyrants? Fear God and me, and fear Him who hath aided you with what ye know \u2014 with cattle and children and gardens and springs.' Then they said, 'Thou hast come to turn us from what our fathers worshipped, and to obtain the chiefdom in the land; we believe thee not.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 26:128-136 combined with 11:50-62 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "3",
        text: "And when the fateful day came upon them, a piercing wind blew during seven nights and eight days, and it laid those people low; and thou mightest have seen them lying prostrate as though they had been trunks of hollow palm-trees. 'Ad believed not their Lord: away with 'Ad, the people of Hud! And We saved him and those who believed with him by Our mercy, from an ignominious chastisement.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 11:58-67, 69:6-7 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "hud"
    ]
