    license: "Public domain (translation 1861)",
    summary: {
      en: "God tries Ibrahim with commands, and he fulfils them. 'I will make thee an imam of men'; 'And of my seed?' \u2014 'My covenant reacheth not the evildoers.' When Ibrahim and Ismail raise the foundations of the house: 'Our Lord, accept it of us; make us Muslims, and our seed a Muslim people; and show us our rites of pilgrimage, and be merciful to us.' And they pray for a messenger in their seed to recite God's signs and teach the Book \u2014 the prayer answered in Muhammad.",
      zh: "\u771F\u4E3B\u4EE5\u6578\u4E8B\u8A66\u6613\u535C\u62C9\u6B23\uFF0C\u4ED6\u5168\u6578\u5C65\u884C\u3002\u300E\u6211\u5FC5\u7ACB\u4F60\u70BA\u773E\u4EBA\u4E4B\u5E2B\u8868\u300F\u2014\u2014\u300E\u6211\u7684\u5B50\u5B6B\u5462\uFF1F\u300F\u2014\u2014\u300E\u6211\u7684\u7D04\u4E0D\u53CA\u4F5C\u60E1\u8005\u3002\u300F\u7236\u5B50\u7BC9\u5929\u623F\u57FA\u77F3\u6642\u7948\u79B1\uFF1A\u300E\u4E3B\u554A\uFF0C\u6C42\u4F60\u6085\u7D0D\uFF1B\u4F7F\u6211\u5011\u9806\u670D\uFF0C\u4F7F\u6211\u5011\u7684\u5B50\u5B6B\u6210\u9806\u670D\u4E4B\u6C11\uFF1B\u6307\u793A\u6211\u5011\u671D\u89B2\u7684\u5100\u7BC0\u3002\u300F\u4E26\u70BA\u5B50\u5B6B\u4E2D\u4E00\u4F4D\u4F7F\u8005\u7948\u79B1\u2014\u2014\u5373\u7A46\u7F55\u9ED8\u5FB7\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "ritual-origin",
      "sacred-place",
      "foundational-legend",
      "prayer",
      "covenant"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Sacred text of a living tradition; the Meccan sanctuary's foundations, celebrated in pilgrimage rites; public-domain translation."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "And when his Lord had tested Ibrahim with certain commands, and he had fulfilled them, He said, 'Verily I will make thee an imam of men.' Said he, 'And of my seed?' God said, 'My covenant reacheth not the evildoers.' And when Ibrahim and Ismail raised the foundations of the house, they prayed, 'Our Lord, accept it of us, for thou art the Hearing, the Knowing. Our Lord, make us Muslims to thee, and of our seed a people of Muslims to thee, and teach us our holy rites, and be turned towards us, for thou art the Relenting One, the Merciful.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 2:124-128 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "'Our Lord, raise up among them a messenger, one of themselves, who shall rehearse thy signs to them and teach them the Book and the Wisdom, and purify them; for thou art the Mighty, the Wise.' And who but a fool would turn from the faith of Ibrahim? Him We chose in this world, and in the next he shall be one of the just.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 2:129-130 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "3",
        text: "When Ibrahim said, 'O my Lord, make this land secure, and turn me and my sons away from the worship of idols; save me and those born to me from worshipping idols. My Lord, forgive me and my parents and all who on the day of account shall enter my house; and forgive the believers, men and women.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 14:35-41 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "ibrahim",
      "ismail"
    ]
