        id: "2",
        text: "Joseph and his father's household wept seven days at the threshing-floor of Atad beyond the Jordan. Then Joseph returned to Egypt, living to see Ephraim's children of the third generation; he told his brethren: 'God will surely remember you, and bring you out of this land... and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.' He died at a hundred and ten and was embalmed and coffined in Egypt \u2014 awaiting the exodus his oath presupposed. Paraphrase of Genesis 50:4-26 (JPS 1917); not verbatim.",
