        id: "1",
        text: "And two young men went to prison with him. One of them said, 'I saw in a dream that I was pressing wine'; and the other said, 'I saw in a dream that I was carrying bread on my head, of which the birds were eating. Tell us its interpretation, for we see that thou art a doer of good.' Yusuf answered, 'O my two fellow-prisoners, many sorts of food are better than these, and the fear of God is better... O my fellow-prisoners, are sundry lords better than the one Almighty, All-powerful God? Those whom ye worship beside Him are mere names which ye and your fathers have invented: God hath sent down no warrant for them. Judgment belongeth to God alone; He hath commanded that ye worship none but Him \u2014 the right faith; but most men know it not.'",
