    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Canonical scripture of a living tradition; quoted from public-domain JPS 1917. The thirteen divine attributes (Exod 34:6-7) are recited in Selichot penitential liturgy."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "And it came to pass, when Moses came down from mount Sinai with the two tables of the testimony in Moses' hand... that Moses knew not that the skin of his face sent forth beams while He talked with him. And when Aaron and all the children of Israel saw Moses, behold, the skin of his face sent forth beams; and they were afraid to come nigh him.",
        note: "Verbatim: JPS 1917, Exodus 34:29-30 (public domain)."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Moses asked: 'I pray Thee, show me Thy glory.' The answer defines visibility itself: 'Thou canst not see My face... I will put thee in a cleft of the rock, and will cover thee with My hand... and thou shalt see My back; but My face shall not be seen.' Then, descending with the second tablets, Moses passed before the LORD proclaiming the thirteen attributes of mercy \u2014 the theological charter Judaism recites in every season of repentance. Paraphrase of Exodus 33:18-23; 34:6-8 (JPS 1917); not verbatim.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Exodus 33:18-23; 34:6-8 (JPS 1917); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
