    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "And the five men that went to spy out the land went up, and came in thither, and took the graven image, and the ephod, and the teraphim, and the molten image; and the priest stood in the entering of the gate with the six hundred men that were girt with weapons of war. ... And they said unto him: 'Hold thy peace, lay thine hand upon thy mouth, and go with us, and be to us a father and a priest; is it better for thee to be priest unto the house of one man, or that thou be priest unto a tribe and a family in Israel?'",
        note: "Verbatim: JPS 1917, Judges 18:17, 19 (public domain), condensed with ellipsis."
      }
    ],
    persons: []
