    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Canonical hadith of a living tradition; presented as a paraphrase of the Arabic original."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "The Prophet said: While I was sleeping I saw myself at the Kaaba, and there was a man beside it going around it. He was tall, with a dark-red complexion, wavy hair, and his two shoulders were like those of a prince; his teeth were like those of a fine ivory comb. Beside him was another man with curly hair and blind in the right eye, resembling Ibn Qatan. The first was walking around the Kaaba, and the other beside him. I asked, 'Who is this man?' It was said, 'He is Ibrahim.' I said, 'And who is the man with him?' It was said, 'He is the Mu'addhin (caller to prayer) of Paradise.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Sahih al-Bukhari, Kitab al-Fitan, no. 7014; not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "The Prophet said: 'I saw in a dream that I was at the Kaaba and saw the one who used to walk beside Bilal.' Then Bilal's call to prayer was heard, and the Prophet said, 'I have seen the Mu'addhin of Paradise, and I have heard the adhan from Bilal who has died.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Sahih al-Bukhari, Kitab al-Fitan, no. 7014 (variant narration of the same dream-cycle); not verbatim."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "muhammad",
      "bilal"
    ]
