      en: "The captives of Badr are divided among the Muslims. Umar urges killing them; Abu Bakr urges ransom, and the Prophet ransoms them. Among them are men of learning: for a captive who could not pay, the Prophet takes as ransom that he teach ten children of Medina to write; it is said that a man ransomed so became one of the first teachers of the written Book.",
