        text: "His last words were heard by Aisha: 'God on high, the Highest Companion' \u2014 and she knew that he had chosen the higher of the two abodes. He was buried where he died, beneath her apartment. Umar refused to believe and drew his sword, till Abu Bakr came to the crowd and said: 'Whoso worshipped Muhammad, Muhammad is dead; whoso worshipped God, God is living and does not die.' And he recited the verse: 'Muhammad is only a messenger; messengers have passed away before him.'",
        note: "Paraphrase of Ibn Ishaq/Ibn Hisham, Sira (Muir 1877); not verbatim."
