      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Build the Ark under Our eyes and Our revelation, and do not speak to Me for the wrongdoers; they shall be drowned. ... Load into it of every species two by two, and your family, except those against whom the word has gone before; and do not speak to Me for those who have done wrong.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 11:37, 40 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim; ellipsis marks omitted verse."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Noah called to his son, who had kept apart: Embark with us, and be not with the unbelievers! He said: I will betake me to a mountain that shall secure me from the water. He said: There is no security today from the decree of God, except for him on whom He shall have mercy; and a wave passed between them, and he was among the drowned. And it was said: O Earth, swallow up thy water; and, O heaven, withhold thy rain. And the waters abated, and the decree was fulfilled, and the Ark rested upon Al-Judi.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 11:42-44 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "3",
        text: "It was said: O Noah, disembark in peace from Us, and blessings on you and on the peoples with you; but there shall be people whom we will suffer to enjoy a brief respite. This is a history of the cities which We narrate to you; some are standing, and others have been cut off. Noah cried: My Lord, leave not one family of the unbelievers on the earth! For if Thou leave them, they will seduce Thy servants and will beget none but ungrateful sinners.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 11:48-49; 71:26-27 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim."
      }
