    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Glory be to Him who carried His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque, whose precincts We have blessed, that We might show him of Our signs; He it is who hears and sees. The Prophet is mounted on Buraq, the steed with the face of a woman and the body of a horse, guided by Gabriel; he leads the prophets in prayer at Jerusalem \u2014 Abraham, Moses, Jesus \u2014 then is raised through the seven heavens, where he meets the fathers of the faith at each gate, until above the Lote-tree of the boundary he draws near 'as two bow-shots or nearer', and the prayer is enjoined upon the believers, fifty bowed down to five by the intercession of Moses.",
        note: "Paraphrase of Qur'an 17:1 (Rodwell 1861); not verbatim. / Paraphrase of the Isra and Mi'raj hadith tradition; not verbatim; composite of Bukhari/Muslim narratives as summarized."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Muhammad said: While I was at the House in a state between sleep and wakefulness, an angel came to me and split open my breast, and washed it with the water of Zamzam in a basin of gold; then a white animal was brought, between a mule and an ass, and I was set upon it, and Gabriel went with me to the Farthest Mosque, and thence upward; and I saw paradise and the fire.",
        note: "Paraphrase of the Mi'raj hadith tradition; not verbatim; paraphrased from the classical accounts."
      }
    ]
