    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Canonical text of the Taoist canon (Nanhua zhenjing); a priority Creation & Cosmology narrative \u2014 the scriptural charter for Taoist cosmogony and for the deification of sages."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "TAO has its laws, and its evidences. It is devoid both of action and of form. It may be transmitted, but cannot be received. It may be obtained, but cannot be seen. Before heaven and earth were, TAO was. It has existed without change from all time. Spiritual beings drew their spirituality therefrom, while the universe became what we can see it now. To TAO, the zenith is not high, nor the nadir low; no point in time is long ago, nor by lapse of ages has it grown old."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Hsi Wei obtained TAO, and so set the universe in order. Fu Hsi obtained it, and was able to establish eternal principles. The Great Bear obtained it, and has never erred from its course. The sun and moon obtained it, and have never ceased to revolve. K'an P'i obtained it, and established the K'un-lun mountains. P'ing I obtained it, and rules over the streams. Chien Wu obtained it, and dwells on Mount T'ai."
      },
      {
        id: "3",
        text: "The Yellow Emperor obtained it, and soared upon the clouds to heaven. Chuan Hs\xFC obtained it, and dwells in the Dark Palace. Y\xFC Ch'iang obtained it, and fixed himself at the North Pole. Hsi Wang Mu obtained it, and settled at Shao Kuang; since when, no one knows; until when, no one knows either. P'\xEAng Tsu obtained it, and lived from the time of Shun until the time of the Five Princes. Fu Y\xFCeh obtained it, and as the Minister of Wu Ting got the empire under his control. And now, charioted upon one constellation and drawn by another, he has been enrolled among the stars of heaven."
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "laozi",
      "huangdi",
      "xiwangmu"
    ]
