    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: "Ibn Muljam, a Kharijite of the breakaway sect, had bound himself to kill Ali, and waited for him in the mosque of Kufa at the dawn prayer of Ramadan. As Ali came out of his couch of sleep and stood at prayer, the man struck him on the crown of the head with a sword dipped in poison.",
        note: "Paraphrase of al-Tabari via Muir, The Caliphate (1891), ch. 21; not verbatim."
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: "Ali cried, 'By the Lord of the Kaaba, I have succeeded.' The wound was mortal. He called his son Hasan, and spoke of the prayer, and of the fear of God, and of the young man who had killed him \u2014 'Kill him gently, if I die of the wound, and do not mutilate him; I heard the Prophet say, do not mutilate even the dog.' And the First of the Muslims to be slain at prayer was buried in Kufa, and the caliphate passed out of the line of the companions.",
        note: "Paraphrase of al-Tabari via Muir, The Caliphate (1891), ch. 21; not verbatim."
      }
    ],
