    license: "Public domain (translation 1889)",
    summary: {
      en: "Yang Tz\u016D Ch\xFC asks whether an ardent, courageous, tireless seeker of the Tao would be a wise ruler. Lao Tz\u016D answers that he would be a mere handicraftsman wearing out body and mind; the tiger suffers from the beauty of his skin. The wise ruler's goodness covers the empire, yet he himself seems to know it not \u2014 it is based upon the baseless, and travels through the realms of Nowhere.",
      zh: "\u967D\u5B50\u5C45\u898B\u8001\u8043\u66F0\uFF1A\u6709\u4EBA\u65BC\u6B64\uFF0C\u56AE\u75BE\u5F37\u6881\uFF0C\u7269\u5FB9\u758F\u660E\uFF0C\u5B78\u9053\u4E0D\u5026\u2014\u2014\u5982\u662F\u8005\u53EF\u6BD4\u660E\u738B\u4E4E\uFF1F\u8001\u8043\u66F0\uFF1A\u660E\u738B\u4E4B\u6CBB\uFF0C\u529F\u84CB\u5929\u4E0B\u800C\u4F3C\u4E0D\u81EA\u5DF1\uFF0C\u5316\u8CB8\u842C\u7269\u800C\u6C11\u5F17\u6043\uFF1B\u7ACB\u4E4E\u4E0D\u6E2C\uFF0C\u800C\u904A\u65BC\u7121\u6709\u8005\u4E5F\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "sacred-kingship",
      "parable-teaching"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Canonical text of the Taoist canon (Nanhua zhenjing). Included as a comparative text \u2014 a scholarly framing, not a claim about religious truth."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: 'Yang Tz\u016D Ch\xFC went to see Lao Tz\u016D, and said, "Suppose a man were ardent and courageous, acquainted with the order and principles of things, and untiring in the pursuit of TAO--would he be accounted a wise ruler?" "From the point of view of a truly wise man," replied Lao Tz\u016D, "such a one would be a mere handicraftsman, wearing out body and mind alike. The tiger and the pard suffer from the beauty of their skins. The cleverness of the monkey, the tractability of the ox, bring them both to the tether. It is not on such grounds that a ruler may be accounted wise."'
      },
      {
        id: "2",
        text: '"The goodness of a wise ruler," answered Lao Tz\u016D, "covers the whole empire, yet he himself seems to know it not. It influences all creation, yet none is conscious thereof. It appears under countless forms, bringing joy to all things. It is based upon the baseless, and travels through the realms of Nowhere."'
      }
    ],
