        id: "1",
        text: "Abu Muslim had made the Abbasid revolution in Khurasan and won Persia for the House. The caliph al-Mansur, grown uneasy before so great a man, summoned him to the court. The friends of Abu Muslim warned him; the astrologers warned him; and he came, saying that he had given thirty years to the House and would not refuse its summons.",
