        id: "1",
        text: "A dervish sat at his door in contentment, and a king passing by offered him wealth. He said, 'Keep thy wealth, for I am rich without it.' The king said, 'How art thou rich?' The dervish said, 'In that I ask nothing of the king.' Saadi's moral is of the free man: the beggar who asks is the poor man, and the man who is contented is the rich \u2014 and the king went away the poorer of the two.",
