        id: "1",
        text: "The jackal Dimna, accused of the ox's death, defended himself with a whole day of eloquence: he cited the law, and the precedent of the wolves, and the necessity of the state, and the mercy that the king had shown to him who had only served him; and the assembly of the beasts was nearly persuaded.",
