    license: "Public domain (translation 1889)",
    summary: {
      en: "Shun asks Yao how he employs his faculties. Yao describes his pity for the orphan and widow; Shun answers that this is good but not great \u2014 be passive like the virtue of God, whose sun and moon shine and seasons revolve without effort. Yao cries out that he has been making a muddle: You are in accord with God; I am in accord with man.",
      zh: "\u821C\u554F\u65BC\u582F\uFF1A\u5929\u738B\u4E4B\u7528\u5FC3\u4F55\u5982\uFF1F\u582F\u66F0\uFF1A\u543E\u4E0D\u6556\u7121\u544A\uFF0C\u4E0D\u5EE2\u7AAE\u6C11\uFF0C\u5609\u5B7A\u5B50\u800C\u54C0\u5A66\u4EBA\u3002\u821C\u66F0\uFF1A\u5929\u5FB7\u800C\u51FA\u5BE7\u2014\u2014\u65E5\u6708\u7167\u800C\u56DB\u6642\u884C\uFF0C\u82E5\u665D\u591C\u4E4B\u6709\u7D93\uFF0C\u96F2\u884C\u800C\u96E8\u65BD\u77E3\u3002"
    },
    motifs: [
      "sacred-kingship",
      "parable-teaching",
      "orphan-hero"
    ],
    sensitivity: {
      restricted: false,
      note: "Canonical text of the Taoist canon (Nanhua zhenjing). Included as a comparative text \u2014 a scholarly framing, not a claim about religious truth."
    },
    passages: [
      {
        id: "1",
        text: 'Of old, Shun asked Yao, saying, "How does your Majesty employ your faculties?" "I am not arrogant towards the defenceless," replied Yao. "I do not neglect the poor. I grieve for those who die. I pity the orphan. I sympathise with the widow. Beyond this, nothing." "Good indeed!" cried Shun, "but yet not great." "How so?" inquired Yao. "Be passive," said Shun, "like the virtue of God. The sun and moon shine; the four seasons revolve; day and night alternate; clouds come and rain falls." "Alas!" cried Yao, "what a muddle I have been making. You are in accord with God; I am in accord with man."'
      }
    ],
    persons: [
      "yao"
    ]
