        text: 'Chuang Tz\u016D and Hui Tz\u016D had strolled on to the bridge over the Hao, when the former observed, "See how the minnows are darting about! That is the pleasure of fishes." "You not being a fish yourself," said Hui Tz\u016D, "how can you possibly know in what consists the pleasure of fishes?" "And you not being I," retorted Chuang Tz\u016D, "how can you know that I do not know?"'
