        text: "The world was all before them, where to choose their place of rest, and Providence their guide: they, hand in hand, with wandering steps and slow, through Eden took their solitary way. The archangel Michael leads the exiled pair up a mount of vision, shows them the history of the world to come, and girds their loins for exile \u2014 'the world was all before them, where to choose their place of rest, and Providence their guide: they, hand in hand, with wandering steps and slow, through Eden took their solitary way.' The last eight lines of the epic made the homeless pair the West's emblem of mortality borne by providence."
