        id: "2",
        text: `"There is no difficulty in winning the people. Love them and they will draw near. Profit them and they will come up. Praise them and they will vie with one another. But introduce something they dislike, and they will be gone. ... Love and profit are born of charity and duty to one's neighbour. Those who ignore charity and duty to one's neighbour are few; those who make capital out of them are many. ... Yao knows that good men benefit the empire. But he does not know that they injure it. Only those on a higher level than good men know this."`
