        id: "1",
        text: "When the Yellow Emperor fought with Yen Ti on the field of P'an-ch'iian, his vanguard was composed of bears, wolves, panthers, lynxes and tigers, while his ensign-bearers were eagles, ospreys, falcons and kites. This was forcible impressment of animals into the service of man. The Emperor Yao entrusted K'uei with the regulation of music."
