        id: "2",
        text: "So then the Queen said, 'Jack, I got one more trial for you to do. If you could go up there in this cornfield and kill all the rice-birds, I let you get married to my daughter.' He went to the field to the rice-birds, and B' Jack said, 'B' Rice-birds, what you no think these foolish people say? They say all of you rice-birds can't fill up this basket!' The rice-birds said, 'Why, people so foolish \u2014 no, all us rice-birds can't fill up that basket!' So all the rice-birds went in the basket, and B' Jack drew the basket together with the rice-birds in it, and went home to the Queen: 'Here the rice-birds.' \u2014 'Well, B' Jack, you can get married to my daughter.' E bo ban, my story's end.",
